	 ('1e7b7275-21de-4819-ae41-9e95811ef1a4'::uuid,'Betting was a major part of the Hunger Trials. It was introduced in the 10th Hunger Games. People from the districts bet on the tributes reaped, with odds given on their ages and other factors.
In the Capitol, betting took place throughout the Games, starting before training and increasing in intensity until a victor is determined. Various statistics are tracked and reported to help people place their bets, such as each tribute''s list of kills. Some people close to the Games, such as head stylists were not allowed to bet. Proceeds from betting were funneled toward the cost of the Games.
Betting activity was high around the opening of each Games, when the initial casualties occurred. However, betting rates further increased after the final eight, when interviews were conducted with the tributes'' families.
Betting was first implemented for the 10th Hunger Games. During the Games, a phone number was made available for betting. The odds list for each tribute was displayed.
Betting played a role in how the tributes conduct themselves. A tribute tried to appear strong in the arena, believing that nobody would bet on a tribute who keeps sniveling over the deaths of opponents.
Odds boards and wager stations displayed the odds of each tribute winning. Odds were continually updated over time. Training scores give the audience a starting point for betting that would continue throughout the Games. An odds list for each tribute was displayed before the Games began.','{"source": "Betting.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 0, "position": 0, "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 1, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Betting.txt", "parent_document_id": "8dafabf3-8a7c-42e1-99a0-eb7501742ce5"}','[0.06721149,0.0434246,-0.0067726877,-0.008570378,0.025700372,-0.01592727,0.00852028,0.008061198,-0.005609627,0.02194682,-0.03549197,0.005007515,0.04340878,-0.014099357,-0.021505538,-0.07868723,0.01149696,0.051905017,-0.05029316,0.018947965,0.024926502,0.062606044,-0.02472079,-0.03602492,0.0014236205,0.00087513874,0.081169665,0.0023329225,-0.13915169,0.01608862,-0.026217405,0.014048832,-0.01685327,0.037513357,-0.04264396,-0.013848425,0.024023043,-0.0021627282,-0.015793364,-0.026413698,0.027025912,0.009983107,0.0005753068,0.0032234068,0.020314237,0.04076306,0.03141294,0.0092905145,-0.028556742,-0.012297865,0.00019821583,-0.023293393,-0.057420213,-0.0123338755,0.023470428,0.00667314,0.0062357686,-0.0029698494,-0.027463617,0.0028375052,-0.027346186,0.014786638,0.0068994644,0.027616343,-0.0036537244,-0.0060677934,-0.02524794,-0.03144085,-0.0030984802,-0.013922535,0.023795802,0.020105883,0.025227657,0.0090496885,0.049717557,-0.035683334,-0.05800942,-0.014855616,0.005864424,0.032953374,0.039461464,-0.03277816,-0.017238172,-0.036093336,0.01853685,-0.021413507,-0.029525636,-0.003332686,-0.033299595,-0.014456696,0.014256491,0.009588349,-0.023310704,0.040625855,0.013102021,0.028742788,-0.01047848,0.03677175,-0.02429119,0.015774235,-0.016539693,-0.007861966,-0.0013168219,-0.006423544,0.038526017,0.014933813,-0.00783716,-0.003286487,-0.0061988398,0.0004949771,-0.025822893,0.01871404,0.0448351,-0.011310393,0.008352807,0.