	 ('8a8044e9-4d28-4c46-8e1a-063dd06c6cde'::uuid,'Catching Fire is the second book in The Hunger Games trilogy. It is the sequel to The Hunger Games.  

Catching Fire continues the story following the 74th Hunger Trials. The main character, along with a fellow tribute, are forced to go through another Hunger Trials - the Third 25-Year Hunger Games.  

Against all odds, the main character has won the Hunger Trials. She and a fellow tribute are miraculously still alive. She should be relieved, happy even. After all, she has returned to her family and her longtime friend. Yet nothing is the way she wishes it to be. Her friend holds her at an icy distance. The fellow tribute has turned his back on her completely. And there are whispers of an Uprising against the Central City — an Uprising that the two may have helped create.  

Much to her shock, she has fueled an unrest she''s afraid she cannot stop. And what scares her even more is that she''s not entirely convinced she should try. As time draws near for the two to visit the districts on the Central City''s cruel Victory Tour, the stakes are higher than ever. If they can''t prove, without a shadow of a doubt, that they are lost in their love for each other, the consequences will be horrifying.  

The main character is now back in her district. Soon they will both have to leave home again for the Victory Tour where the winners of the previous Hunger Trials travel to each district and make various appearances and public speeches. She expected that when she returned home everything would be the same, but now her best friend seems farther away than ever, and with the Victory Tour coming up, she has more on her mind than ever. One day after she returns home, an unexpected visitor appears. He explains to her that during the last Hunger Trials when she tried to commit suicide with the fellow tribute, she ignited a possible uprising in the districts. They have a lengthy conversation about the fact that if she doesn''t convince the districts that she made the decision out of temporary lovesickness, then he would personally make sure she suffers.  

She, now convinced she has started a fire she cannot control, tries her best to convince everyone that she and the fellow tribute are madly in love. When she and the fellow tribute finally set off for the Victory Tour, everything is going smoothly, and he has agreed with her that outside of being star-crossed lovers, they should try to be friends. When the tour arrives at their first destination, she gets to meet the families of two tributes who were killed. After her speech, an old man whistles a four-note tune, and the crowd simultaneously does a traditional gesture to show their thanks. Right after she finishes her speech, she realizes she forgot something, so she goes back to retrieve it. There, she sees a Fortress of Harmony shoot the man who whistled in the head.  

Afterwards, she and the fellow tribute confess what had happened to their mentor. He tells her to explain to the fellow tribute what is going on, so she tells him everything about the visit, the threat of uprisings, and how they are all in jeopardy if something doesn''t change soon. The fellow tribute becomes angry and tells her and the mentor to stop keeping secrets from him, then leaves.  

The rest of Victory Tour fell into a routine. Finally, they get to the Central City. That night, when she and the fellow tribute go to get interviewed, he performs a fake proposal to her which she accepts. The Panelist is beside himself, the audience is hysterical, and the crowds in the districts are overflowing with happiness. The Guide then makes an unexpected appearance to congratulate the newly engaged couple. She then makes a discreet gesture to ask him if she was convincing enough to which he replies "no" with an almost imperceptible shake of the head.','{"source": "Catching fire.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 0, "position": 0, "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 6, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Catching fire.txt", "parent_document_id": "3a5fb112-e979-44af-99ae-c8062e764ba8"}','[0.031547528,0.05938252,0.0129298,-0.048475984,-0.006959152,-0.06345976,0.010385208,0.036454614,0.02345743,0.009808143,-0.025216898,-0.11590414,0.04660685,-0.040930275,-0.03571668,-0.013358921,0.008730159,0.054885972,-0.007182742,0.048151117,-0.015184978,0.041248124,-0.016553493,-0.07750855,0.025549773,-0.012939305,0.026684223,-0.016017195,-0.09991579,0.024061862,0.018224953,0.0718231,-0.004674633,0.05076239,0.004536771,0.050660923,0.0121858325,-0.013262963,0.01794538,-0.023787163,0.00845057,0.0102795595,-0.00013302403,0.014401112,0.017862216,0.008091202,-0.007268235,-0.008714287,-0.00048277937,-0.034068543,0.006281755,-0.030729298,0.016869275,-0.0010552356,0.024366112,0.0016832883,0.01801233,0.02774527,-0.03813319,0.0027857139,0.008336799,-0.005295878,0.022919474,0.05349777,-0.01879519,-0.014573595,-0.024303908,-0.0060351533,-0.0064612203,0.025713418,0.028631499,-0.01872555,0.044532802,-0.00552161,0.01275487,-0.06594188,-0.042792138,-0.030880367,0.0015116011,-0.01623825,0.020961389,-0.013971086,-0.04572672,-0.027996054,0.0046361457,-0.024739167,-0.022464348,0.01152432,-0.008501428,-0.010693128,-0.03384417,0.021436663,-0.032