8783,0.021166252,0.00028609496,-0.014283487,-0.026856069,-0.03887555,0.016924717,-0.008485605,0.017329669,0.034548685]'::public.vector),
	 ('900e4d60-3239-4b9b-a617-af8a5b9b39c6'::uuid,'She now knows her life is in constant danger, but despite that, she feels somewhat relieved, and carries on like nothing ever happened.  

That night, she has dinner in the mansion and feasts like never before. Many Central City citizens drank something that made them vomit so they could eat more. Soon it''s time to go and they are on their way back to their district. She suffers from terrifying nightmares throughout the night on the train, so the fellow tribute sleeps in her bed to calm her and keep her company. Finally they get back and a huge party is thrown for them. While in a home, she sees on a television that there is an uprising going on in another district. She arranges a secret meeting with her friend, at which he confesses his love for her but she says that she does not have those feelings for him. Her friend gets angry and disappointed but before he leaves she accidentally tells him there was an Uprising. Her friend then says that they could have an Uprising in their district as well, and he runs off to spread the news. She then goes to the fellow tribute to ask him if he would run away with her and he says yes, but while they are discussing the plans, they see that her friend is being violently whipped in the square by an unfamiliar man.  

She steps in to stop the man, but he gives her a lash across the face. She gets severely hurt but the mentor and the fellow tribute step in to save her. Eventually the people convince the man to stop whipping her friend. As soon as he leaves, everyone helps her take her friend to her mother. Her mother tries to soothe the pain by giving him medicine when suddenly another person comes with some morphling to help soothe the pain. Later on that night, she says she picks her friend, but is still torn between him and the fellow tribute.  

The next day, there is a huge blizzard, during which the man constructs several stockades, an official whipping post, and a gallows, as well as a series of machine gun positions perched on the rooftops in the square. While walking in town, the mentor and the two see these ugly tools of torture, and then a local place is destroyed by the Sentinel Corps. The last thing she notices when leaving the square is that she does not recognize even one of the Sentinel Corps'' faces.  

She realizes that she cannot stand to be at home, so she goes into the woods. She sees two Sentinel Corps, and before she shoots them, one of them holds up a cracker with a mockingjay on it.  

The two Sentinel Corps were actually two young women who had run away from another district. They brought news to her about the uprising in their district. They said they were headed to another district which, to her, was unbelievable. They believe that people lived underground there. They explain to her that they know it exists because the Central City reuses old footage whenever it is shown on Television, as they believe that they always see the same bird in the same place. This leads her to wonder what the district currently looks like.  

She gives the women her food supplies and shows them how to hunt. When the evening comes, they leave her and she returns. However she realizes that the fence to the district is now electrified and she is unable to enter through her normal passage. She decides she needs to go over the fence, and searches for the right tree. She climbs up and over and must jump from a great height. She lands, and hurts herself. She returns home and tells her family that her slipping on some ice caused her injuries, but there are two peacekeepers there waiting for her. They are surprised to see her, because they know she was in the forest and believed she would be trapped on the other side of the fence.  

They were waiting for her not to show up so they can bring her family in for questioning.','{"source": "Catching fire.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 6, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Catching fire.txt", "parent_document_id": "3a5fb112-e979-44af-99ae-c8062e764ba8"}','[-0.0022773512,0.07306315,-0.0050584893,0.017197948,0.0019186343,-0.05899572,0.033232138,-0.0009958298,0.012087101,0.018198317,-0.03865948,-0.083646655,0.045206297,-0.056987718,-0.016549472,0.020622892,0.016742356,0.04880051,-0.006146273,0.06991432,0.028096111,0.03313033,-0.0031364455,-0.104223356,0.020623805,0.0031380574,0.018675104,-0.032497264,-0.11075494,0.030702546,0.031972934,0.029372178,0.01674933,0.04723154,0.015996756,0.021410592,0.013039288,0.007092477,0.046718262,-0.04045578,0.041050717,0.018371819,-0.016808335,0.012711978,0.0019056799,-0.0060680886,0.00030809062,-0.024818387,0.012743526,-0.04122391,0.023406096,-0.02863245,0.025713017,0.009607934,0.035880674,0.022289218,-0.005426541,0.0214662,-0.023340166,0.0005764651,-0.003779682,-0.019286433,-0.012716115,0.024413075,0.029005984,-0.021592144,0.008114956,-0.0056972494,0.001239335,-0.023700334,0.01812749,0.011688815,0.013312768,0.0159781,0.019814221,-0.045768917,-0.07209577,-0.039739713,-0.023932599,0.0130251665,-0.0012015707,-0.009074559,-0.032326527,-0.0140787475,0.029608106,-0.030183418,-0.011307285,0.002844488,-0.008189886,0.009908031,-0.03654303,0.0002830032,-0.012444587,0.042688783,0.022154843,-0.020211875,-0.026200952,-0.010308674,-0.034103822,0.008739523,-0.02066821,0.04756584,0.00068116974,-0.019808277,-0.008243883,-0.051080108,0.0063521266,-0.044757046,-0.0028398514,-0.019063348,-0.024305372,-0.023477098,0.005487981,0.025574585,-0.018935075,-0.02375382,-0.010220653,0.035437904,-0.015502608,0.041387442,0.008515546,0.0071983226,-0.0066409865,0.017048158,0.020294454,-0.0014006064,-0.004505734,0.0098462785,0.008984683,0.0357