	 ('ecf00186-b407-46d1-acaa-36c489701dbc'::uuid,'Luckily, the mentor, the fellow tribute and her sibling were able to go along with a story to cover for her. After the Sentinel Corps leave, her mother examines her broken foot, and the fellow tribute stays with her through the night after she asked him to stay. She is in bed for the winter, while he keeps her company and they enter information in her mothers'' medicinal and edible plant book, with pictures that he is drawing.  

Once she is healed, her Makeover crew comes in to help her with her Wedding Shoot, along with her stylist. She listens to them speak of how they have not had shrimp in the Central City for weeks and realizes that other districts are rebelling. The next day, she speaks to the mentor and he tells her that because their district is so small, everyone would need to join in for them to overthrow the Sentinel Corps and the Central City. The same day, her sibling comes home and tells everyone that there is a mandatory television scheduling that night, which she believes is the footage from the Wedding Shoot.  

Her sibling is partially correct, but there is also another big announcement. The Guide appears with a wooden box, and reminds the audience of the dark days and when the Hunger Trials were born. He also states that every 25 years, the anniversary of the Hunger Trials is marked by a 25-Year Hunger Games, a glorified version of the Games. He talks about the first 25-Year Hunger Games, when every district was made to vote on who was sent to the Hunger Trials. In the second 25-Year Hunger Games, every district was forced to send twice as many tributes into the Hunger Trials. The wooden box holds the information for the 3rd 25-Year Hunger Games. He pulls out an envelope and states that the male and female tributes will be reaped from the existing pool of victors. Since her district has only three winners, the fellow tribute, the mentor, and herself, she knows that she is now going to be forced to go back to the Hunger Trials.  

She runs out of the house and into a basement of an empty house to scream and cry. She makes her way to the mentor where he already tells her the fellow tribute has come to visit him, and told him that he wants to go back into the arena to protect her. She tells the mentor that whatever they do, she wants him to make sure the fellow tribute comes back alive. She and the mentor get drunk and the next afternoon, she goes back to the mentor''s house where the fellow tribute has emptied all of his liquor and has threatened to turn them or anyone who gives them alcohol in. He tells them that they will be training for the 25-Year Hunger Games because two people will come back alive, and they begin to work out and also study footage of past winners to see their competition.  

On the day of the reaping, she has decided to say goodbye to her friend, to tell him how much he means to her. The reaping has her as only choice for the female competitor, and the male competitor chosen is the mentor; however, the fellow tribute volunteers to take his place. Instead of being able to tell their families goodbye, they are brought directly to the train and leave for the Central City.  

Once at the Central City, they eat and find out who the competitors from the other districts are. That night, after she is woken from a nightmare, she goes to see the fellow tribute. The two embrace and are interrupted. They decide to watch more videos and come across the mentor''s victory from the 2nd 25-Year Hunger Games which they have not seen. She recognizes a name as her mother''s friend, and realizes that she was a twin to her friend''s mother. She also sees her mother crying and embracing the friend when she is called. She also sees the mentor being called up. She notes that he was powerful looking, and even somewhat handsome.','{"source": "Catching fire.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 2, "position": 2, "chunk_index": 2, "total_chunks": 6, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Catching fire.txt", "parent_document_id": "3a5fb112-e979-44af-99ae-c8062e764ba8"}','[0.05159175,0.066100895,0.013107945,-0.045857836,0.009439532,-0.034075394,0.01091311,0.026101654,0.008888531,0.038219113,-0.045458354,-0.05790611,0.05729811,-0.029282311,-0.03212984,-0.04002716,-0.01835162,0.053076684,-0.016530367,0.051759142,0.024082543,0.043059077,0.018169858,-0.089576684,0.029590478,-0.018438619,0.035920344,-0.020867258,-0.12821452,0.012861201,-0.006034536,0.029860936,0.0053137396,0.036213182,-0.0017064303,0.019002536,0.00916701,0.0008269394,0.013399083,-0.025269527,0.020617237,0.027786452,-0.014471354,0.005091087,0.022916581,0.021156294,0.0288998,-0.0018249096,-0.0044684936,-0.020008774,0.018428769,-0.03912653,-0.024813363,0.010274087,0.03432527,0.02558462,-0.0036877024,0.028208086,-0.030471755,-0.00017194432,-0.022671811,-0.001418104,0.015306232,0.051836584,0.028726563,-0.017623486,0.02373826,-0.0024655203,-0.025569689,0.0048808167,0.02248862,0.00053137686,0.020942817,0.032697733,0.013316549,-0.060316365,-0.06551569,-0.03660964,-0.010547967,0.029952036,0.016292127,-0.015667707,-0.012097439,-0.044045508,0.015834406,-0.042793933