	 ('3a7997cb-f8b3-4cff-98e3-a78ae381866f'::uuid,'When he heard the jabberjays targeting him, he called out for his true love, a victor who went insane after witnessing her district partner decapitated during her Hunger Trials. He believed that his lover was being tortured or killed, debilitated by his helplessness. She killed the jabberjay, but this didn''t calm him, who was still unnerved by the thought that his love had been tortured to make those sounds. After he and she escaped the attack, her ally reassured the two of them that the Hunger Trials are down to the final eight—and not only must the Capitol have family and friends to interview, but that those sounds could be faked. Another ally concurred, explaining that it would be easy to fake the sounds. The alliance viewed the faces of the tributes that died the second day. He suffered another night of restless sleep, occasionally murmuring his love''s name.

He assisted with a plan, along with her ally, while she and another set up a trap. After the line was cut and another removed her tracker—in what seemed like a vicious attack at the time—he chased an attacker to get her away. She aimed her arrows at him, who reminded her who the real enemy was. Moments later, she destroyed the arena.

Afterward, he and others were rescued by a hovercraft. It was revealed that he and another were part of a plan to overthrow the Capitol all along. After she awakened she went to the room where he and others were talking. There, she learned about the rebels and the plan to overthrow the Capitol. He stopped her from attacking another with her nails. He tells her that he wished the others would just die so that they wouldn''t have to suffer anymore.

He became deeply distressed, slightly unhinged, and unable to focus on anything but to save his true love, who had been kidnapped and was being tortured. One of the ways he kept himself sane was by repeatedly knotting short lengths of rope. When she first saw him, she called for him but received no response. She shook him, and he quickly stopped tying knots and gripped her hand in relief to see a familiar face. He asked why they were meeting here and she informed him about her role and her conditions. He was happy to hear about his condition for the immunity of victors because his love would be protected.

He visited her and had dinner with her. He comforted her since she was stressed, then the two watched propaganda. She asked him to shut it off but stopped when an interview with her ally came on. After the interview, he tried to calm her down and pretended not to have seen the interview. The next day, he and she went to the woods to hunt, discussing the interview together. After another interview, the entire district evacuated to safe bunkers before it was bombed. During the bombing, he gave her her own rope to distract herself with. That night, she told him her thoughts on the President''s plan. He told her he was doing the same with him but with his love. He revealed the first time he realized she did love her ally and admitted he misjudged her.

Eventually, a rescue team saved his love, her ally, and the others. To distract from the rescue mission, he and she performed a live interview to be broadcast. During this interview, he revealed his backstory after his Hunger Trials, where he was forced into sex trafficking. Upon hearing his story, indicating his promiscuity was just an act, she realized she misjudged him and regretted it immensely. He revealed that instead of money, he asked for secrets from his lovers. He also revealed that the President strategically poisoned political allies in order to remain in power.

He waited with her until they were informed that the rescue party had arrived. He and his love embraced each other and he took her to receive medical attention, as she had been tortured. They married shortly afterward and conceived a son.','{"source": "Finnick Odair.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 2, "position": 2, "chunk_index": 2, "total_chunks": 4, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Finnick Odair.txt", "parent_document_id": "c948dc16-091c-4f46-bf41-ba092a3734a1"}','[0.008621476,0.037647158,0.054377247,0.009902597,0.015575448,-0.07356806,0.027472647,0.013463572,-0.02094138,0.017563982,-0.064321496,-0.055151153,0.023243438,-0.021495117,-0.05343408,0.003394305,0.055147305,0.015417502,0.0067805625,0.05200672,-0.025950117,0.018810634,0.011162301,-0.073782004,0.042902105,0.004880177,0.034341455,-0.012732447,-0.10759895,0.0017479614,-0.020980436,0.03839119,0.0028356991,0.04320168,0.009727788,0.032592963,0.018068116,0.015888417,0.0027457196,-0.045764983,0.002690812,0.02225879,0.009403945,0.011556708,0.024220703,0.009783553,0.01729725,-0.02325493,-0.029674362,-0.023459237,-0.007951247,-0.031131594,0.003005109,-0.00791516,0.057283968,0.0031594331,0.011488441,0.030091135,-0.03635933,-0.00073566375,-0.015641822,-0.0028884476,-0.004142105,0.010872838,0.014376699,-0.041549906,-0.008173784,-0.03106928,0.017135797,-0.0031444035,0.024689302,-0.012299713,0.017425165,0.008575367,0.031904913,-0.06621399,-0.06592506,-0.030169657,0.019038673,0.012002268,0.0064388383,-0.027595628,-0.008021433,-0.023190135,0.024888797,-0.056369748,-0.00059252814,9.1646354e-05,-0.016615896,-0.006409146,-0.015041537,-0.0093785105,0.020858904,0.023284184,0.022955006,-0.026674056,-0.009752934,0.027537374,-0.024728535,-0.014166262,0.011675089,0.039275836,-0.037441485,0.0030662497,0.0046745995,-0.017124161,-0.000805429,-0.025685849,0.011171432,-0.025698666,-0.013940705,0.014039276,0.0079566045,0.005715483,-0.011102596,-0.029954351,-0.008419815,0.01995