	 ('4f0e93ce-0c7d-4678-a858-a85a2ad32f02'::uuid,'She stabbed the dreamer in the cheek and then turned into a mutt and began to lick the wound, causing great pain. Lena reminded her that she couldn''t run away from her fears, thereafter turning into a mutt and giving chase.

During the Games, Lena stabbed a male tribute during the bloodbath. She targeted another tribute next, aiming a knife at her head, but it was blocked. She was the only Career tribute who came close to killing a specific tribute twice, and certainly seemed to have a deep hatred for her, perhaps because that tribute received a higher score.

In the Games, Lena, being a Career Tribute, had medicine, food, water, weapons and other supplies. The supplies were destroyed from mines. When they were blown up, she was left with her knives and whatever she had left in her pack. In an adaptation, after the bloodbath, she retrieved a small array of knives on a vest, which she wore until she died. She also had a large pocket full of big knives. The smallest knife was the one she pulled out to try and kill a tribute at the feast.

Lena had a large selection of knives, which were attached to the inside of her jacket. The weapons gave Lena a big advantage because of her skill with knives. In both the Training Hub and during the Games, she proved herself to be able to both throw them accurately and use them in close combat, as shown when she forced a tribute into submission. She, along with the other Careers, had her choice of weapons to use, until the supplies were destroyed.

Lena was strong, sadistic, arrogant, violent, dangerous, and powerful, characteristics of a typical Career. Lena was also slightly unhinged, which made her a feared opponent. She had a strong hatred for a specific tribute, particularly due to her higher score from the Gamemakers. When she captured that tribute, she boasted about how her team killed another tribute and joyfully stated she was going to make her death a slow and painful one, exemplifying her psychotic and sadistic nature.

Lena was also intelligent, supporting an idea to keep a tribute alive to get to another, and was smart enough to go to a lake to heal her tracker jacker wounds, and was also instinctive enough to go back to the Cornucopia instead of chasing a tribute. While Lena was confident in her abilities to hold her own and take on other tributes, this facade collapsed when faced with overwhelming force. Completely terrified, Lena was too cowardly to own up to her mockery when at his mercy and ultimately was only able to scream for help in her final moments.

Lena, like most Careers, was strong, healthy, brawny and fit. In the source material, she was described as being heavier than another tribute. It was heavily implied that Lena was larger. In a nightmare, Lena turned into a wolf mutt with dark fur sprouting from her skin. With the wolf mutts fur resembling the tributes hair it is likely that Lena herself had dark hair. In an adaptation, Lena was smaller and younger, had dark hair, usually in a ponytail or braid, dark eyes, and some freckles.

Lena and her district partner were allies. During the feast, her ally showed concern for Lena and distress at her death. As her ally ran toward a mortally wounded Lena, his voice sounded pained, and despite its futility, he begged Lena to stay with him as she died. Though both were cruel toward the other tributes, they had formed an emotional connection with each other. However, in an adaptation, they seemed to have no relationship with each other beyond that of allies. Her ally did not come to Lena''s aid during the feast, although she screamed his name.

