	 ('162c476d-8d1f-4cb2-bff6-140768f2561d'::uuid,'Peter Morrow is the deuteragonist of The Fire Games. He is a baker''s son from District 7 who is reaped for the 74th Hunger Trials alongside the female protagonist. During the Games, he and his fellow tribute pretend to be star-crossed lovers to gain sponsors, a performance where his feelings are genuine but hers are not entirely. This act allows them to both become victors by defying the Gamemakers'' rules.

He is captured following a subsequent Hunger Trials and subjected to a form of psychological torture that distorts his memories, making him believe his fellow tribute is a threat. He eventually recovers from this conditioning. Over time, the relationship between the two evolves from a performed romance into a genuine one. They eventually marry and have two children.

Physically, he is described as having blond hair, blue eyes, and a stocky build. He loses part of his leg due to an injury sustained in the first Games.

His personality is kind, gentle, and charismatic. He is clever with words and a skilled public speaker, but is generally non-violent and reluctant to fight. He is selfless, often willing to sacrifice himself for others. His abilities include strength, hand-to-hand combat, and exceptional skill in deception and public persuasion. He is also a talented artist, skilled in painting and cake decorating.

Following the war, he returns to his district and helps create a memorial book to remember those lost, finding a measure of peace.','{"source": "Peeta Mellark.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 0, "position": 0, "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 1, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Peeta Mellark.txt", "parent_document_id": "b6ea7aa7-c0c8-433d-ac82-577aa2a7cf28"}','[0.0010708019,0.07138665,0.018948311,-0.021673905,-0.011814204,-0.09859651,0.021640925,0.01463513,0.031437922,0.017583016,-0.05111675,-0.05088472,0.058201086,0.0045661554,-0.07661437,0.010651228,0.062352944,0.017864788,0.013805352,0.05262151,-0.04812262,0.025556348,0.0032340344,-0.051152784,-0.002684062,0.021201799,0.058990326,0.0071130027,-0.073352456,-0.018939452,0.034444854,0.0031432877,-0.021136612,0.0201417,0.018255789,0.024666697,0.029384492,0.008591441,-0.004329816,-0.012196221,4.75041e-05,0.010604389,0.006907885,0.0055847326,0.0138314115,-0.01771978,0.0068526682,-0.02768822,0.020288445,-0.037718236,0.022009395,-0.02135882,0.021057846,0.020725202,0.045039617,-0.004030863,0.0029767768,-0.0032356875,-0.01820049,0.025896458,-0.004794188,-0.0064937472,0.01963964,0.02371611,-0.016835775,-0.03625558,-0.014050502,-0.013723423,-0.033668578,0.01100348,0.02914584,-0.02812507,0.03569441,-0.033006746,-0.040041547,-0.07770853,-0.032846216,-0.02113906,0.015470542,-0.020730257,0.018189495,-0.016269619,-0.059024543,-0.017565949,-0.022646107,-0.005435284,-0.009139607,-0.001425727,-0.00436075,0.03682138,-0.010475811,0.05370367,-0.010785849,0.02888647,0.030379735,-0.016522389,0.07170378,0.011223384,-0.019057296,0.037878603,-0.002241861,0.04814057,-0.03001002,0.008733317,-0.015555234,-0.026031476,-0.00023324232,-0.04928241,0.011057235,-0.04971629,0.013219527,0.008105154,0.03550836,0.027728885,-0.01717107,-0.010700819,-0.010652839,-0.0035230296,0.0044491813,0.049061332,-0.0029483389,-0.004673201,0.021883914,0.062346324,0.00063233945,-0.01968551,-0.037982915,0.0158