	 ('f4b0c41f-691d-4d23-9393-feef36badf81'::uuid,'According to an observer, these new installations were in frequent use, but it''s unknown whether anyone was executed.

After a victor was rescued from the Capital, the President televised the execution of that victor''s stylist and prep team. By the end of the Second Rebellion, all stylists from a specific Quarter Quell were dead, and all but one prep team had been killed. In that same time frame, all but seven Hunger Games victors were killed in a purge. Many died in a specific Hunger Games, and for most of the subsequent deaths, it''s unknown how many of them were executions, civilian deaths, or casualties of combat.

In a speech, the President announced that possessing images of a mockingjay would be considered treason, punishable by death. While this happened, two people from one district and three from another were hauled out in front of their respective Justice Buildings and a crowd of their peers. With sacks over their faces, each victim was shot once in the back of the head. They are often presumed to be victors due to the purge.

Following the end of the war, the President was tried and sentenced to death. The plan was for him to be shot in the heart with a single arrow by a victor, symbolically firing the last shot of the war. However, she changed her target at the last second and assassinated the Interim President instead. In the ensuing chaos, the former President was either trampled to death by the crowd or choked on his own blood.

According to the Interim President, hundreds of the former President''s accomplices were also awaiting death sentences at the time of his execution, but it is unknown how many of these were actually carried out, if any, under her successor. It is also unknown whether capital punishment was retained or repealed afterwards.','{"source": "Execution.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 2, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Execution.txt", "parent_document_id": "d3b4192a-22c6-4d15-9117-c2e2402750a7"}','[-0.0262581,0.1009061,-0.020952085,0.021983862,-0.0132990945,0.0038086844,0.0015409876,0.021778448,-0.056286015,-0.045707654,-0.083620906,-0.057855748,0.05810234,-0.058964122,-0.011051584,-0.019624457,0.026287818,0.02973502,-0.026865752,0.047024522,-0.022517933,0.040186148,-0.013151461,-0.066423155,0.006961318,-0.0037348631,0.011399026,-0.007937834,-0.097008556,0.008129563,0.02627682,0.0045434586,-0.0041869367,0.04034807,0.0010546786,0.0036864695,0.010773423,0.004531055,-0.0032896546,0.0129645085,0.0046789055,-0.021838445,0.03199094,0.0032069974,0.009105235,-0.01003608,-0.0017096953,-0.029287428,0.0050238287,-0.03267888,-0.0015158309,-0.045574643,0.0035186317,-0.010768994,0.04139975,0.021816282,0.0059753605,0.040661424,-0.017662058,0.0010306734,-0.046871144,0.01072413,-0.023518363,0.014011256,-0.0021916602,-0.024231333,0.0027121776,-0.027979301,0.020441413,0.016515277,0.028348776,-0.03875133,-0.005320635,0.0001205249,0.01487669,-0.040630147,-0.048087027,-0.0310499,0.023617886,-0.0037840945,0.02374751,-0.019893648,-0.005983876,-0.05495046,0.040356826,-0.05789848,-0.029246775,-0.0015107082,0.004769909,-0.0031718474,-0.044735,-0.0011899249,0.0044260705,0.02355717,-0.004741666,-0.040139947,-0.015697263,0.012021755,-0.025129544,0.005794935,0.020760888,0.021406896,-0.0068163536,-0.0054531884,0.009900402,0.0069563123,-0.009438162,0.010998003,0.017366312,-0.013872145,-0.037986