	 ('1c61e1e3-fcd5-475e-823b-572e1a77fa84'::uuid,'This gave a little more money, but left him less time to hunt. He still made time to hunt on Sundays with his friend. His poaching was stopped after he and his friend got into a heated argument. He was caught with a fresh turkey. He was forced to admit his guilt and was then whipped horribly. The other participant was with his friend when the two witnessed the whipping. The other participant had told his friend to leave, knowing full well that she would try to stop it but even with his warning, she rushed to his aid, getting lashed herself in the process. The other participant and another person had to step in. The whipping was soon brought to an end and he was rushed for medical treatment. His friend was by his side during the treatment and kissed him, which brought him back to consciousness. His friend then decides that he is the one she will love. Both had to stop their treks into the woods when the new peacekeeper decides to run constant electricity through the fence.

He works particularly closely with a weapons designer, designing weaponry, and later goes in as a soldier on the ground to assassinate the ruling leader. He eventually moves to another district, where he continues working for the military.

He enjoys a good laugh when he is with his best friend. He can be easy to anger, and often it is his friend who keeps it under control. He hated the ruling power more than most people. He frequently complained about the unjust political situation and the tyranny, in contrast to his friend, who was taught to hold her tongue. He mentions several times that he feels that a rebellion would be better than just doing what the ruling power wanted.

Unlike his friend, he believed in the idea of victory at any cost. He clashed with her over the way the rebellion should be fought. Where she wanted to save as many lives as possible at the risk of defeat, he wanted them to sacrifice a few lives so that they can insure victory. His friend tries to think in short-term, while he thinks in long-term, about how best to preserve life. This ruthlessness, combined with his hatred causes him to become a leading figure in the rebellion and to come up with new combat tactics. Unfortunately, it is also this personality that eventually costs him his relationship with his friend.

He often thinks in black and white terms, meaning something is either wrong or right and rarely does he see a grey area. He is angered that his friend worries for her captive prep team as they are from the ruling power, and so are the ''enemy'' even though they are relatively innocent.

He also had a very idealistic personality. When he believed in something that was being challenged he wouldn''t hesitate to fight for it. It is later said by his friend that his fire, his passion, and personality, was very similar to her own; however, hers was always more controlled. He often accompanied his friend when she did appearances as the rebellion''s symbol, fighting when they came under attack. He also is the first to volunteer for the mission to save the other participant.

He is an expert at snares and strategy. He has known about snares since the first time he went into the woods. He has been able to catch many animals in his snares, which has been helpful for him and his family. He taught his friend about basic snares, which came in handy during the competition. Later, he is able to transfer his skill in snares into a skill in designing military weapons and tactics.

He is also able to use a bow and arrow, though he is not as accurate or fast as his friend. He is able to shoot from a certain distance and it takes him a little longer to shoot, but he is proficient enough to hunt and defend himself.

During the rebellion, he uses a lethal bow, loaded with a variety of gadgets and equipped with three different types of arrows: razor sharp, incendiary, and explosive.','{"source": "Gale Hawthorne.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 3, "position": 3, "chunk_index": 3, "total_chunks": 5, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Gale Hawthorne.txt", "parent_document_id": "21055cb7-aa05-49e5-9d9b-f49624485bb3"}','[0.022555437,0.045794178,0.014501827,0.031068444,0.015249719,-0.054497417,0.0010252304,-0.006444048,-0.00070676167,-0.005288527,-0.106231116,-0.024329038,0.04725329,-0.022642232,-0.024848603,0.026687192,0.057242848,0.016695408,0.004099906,0.0756637,0.021538287,0.030104063,0.012067695,-0.08182366,-0.016181197,0.004582786,0.06250447,-0.00693787,-0.10004366,0.018875634,0.048888993,-0.020859625,-0.013764409,0.018816285,0.017782537,0.030933773,0.016781457,0.026352268,0.018192798,-0.034668244,0.02373778,0.017275875,0.0131063135,-0.00052759086,-0.013992634,-0.009467323,-0.002196159,0.02144544,-0.0005709761,-0.005539387,0.045981545,-0.043337554,0.019097522,-0.0026214335,0.036948416,0.002995097,-0.015928173,0.018694317,-0.0034520759,0.013091196,0.0060626986,0.00060771697,0.0034878827,-0.010161467,-0.008525042,-0.016769229,-0.03961898,-0.018455876,0.0066705486,0.019181756,0.013511107,0.007928252,0.004595763,-0.0004589952,0.0041148965,-0.08077706,-0.080720454,-0.050226204,-0.02242236,-0.005121614,0.015064151,-0.0104586985,-0.029381689,-0.032453056,0.055657294,-0.026077673,-0.019993968,-0.0023521436,-0.002836295,0.016861029,-0.030357148,0.024390513,0.0031416335,0.00732663,0.029488882,-0.0018475305,0.005312988,0.00575757,-0.019062102,0.0019203412,0.0017946512,0.038625825,-0.019392084,-0.0006997877,-0.03532609,-0.0053347447,0.0006061334,-0.018586982,0.03471175,-0.003947136,-0.0034641558,0.012646837,0.019165365,0.0046273945,-0.026566764,-0.017504733,-0.014020023,0.056586128,-0.010110748,0.048163164,-0.0008660409,-0.0025990386,