	 ('8d819921-7847-4886-b7a8-f4a59bc320dd'::uuid,'He was confused at first, and got distracted from the bread he received. The drone was normal for a while, but then suddenly attempted to make another delivery. More drones came and did the same, injuring his eye. He attempted to escape the drones'' torment, and gripped towards the pole he left the crying tribute to when the snake mutts were unleashed. In the process, he put pressure on his injured knee and lost his balance. This caused him to fall, snapping his neck.

While he was being attacked, the other male tribute managed to climb down the scoreboard to attempt another try to kill the crying tribute. Right after his death, the male tribute brought his axe down on her skull, killing her instantly. The drones sent for her were taken by him. After he took a dozen parcels, he left for the barricade. This left three tributes. The remaining tribute proceeded to take the two bodies over to the rest, using a new piece of flag to cover them.

The final female tribute finally came out just before noon and surveyed the arena. She poisoned a puddle with another water bottle with rat poison, receiving many drones of sponsor gifts. She saw the other tribute, so she went the opposite way and checked which tributes were left alive. The male tribute attempted to ambush her, but she ran away on time. Just as he swung at her, she flung herself and clung to him, surprising him. She then grabbed a surviving snake mutt from her dress pockets and the snake bit his neck, killing him. Before he died, he managed to kill the snake mutt by smashing it into the ground multiple times.

As the day grew longer, the hot sun dried up the many puddles. She received more food and water. She later attempted to drag his body to the others, but the remaining tribute shouted at her. She let go and went to the tunnels. He then transported the body himself, satisfied. She then put her plan into motion. Using the fact he had not eaten much for many days, she tired him out by taking the flag pieces, getting him to chase after her. He was very insistent on keeping the corpses covered, and ran ragged to the point of exhaustion. He then desperately drank out of the puddle she had poisoned. He only just made it to the body and covered up only half of himself with a flag before his body gave out. After thirty minutes, she came from the bleachers to check his pulse and, finding nothing, closed his eyelids. She was then announced as the victor of the The Hunger Trials: Ten.

These early Games lacked several features which would become prominent in later versions, while others were experimental. Nobody was said to be a “Career tribute” and there were no known volunteers. The tributes were not injected with trackers, so there was no easy way to tell at any given time if they were alive or dead if they didn''t come out into the open. This had never been a problem before due to the openness of the arena, but became an issue in these Games due to the hiding places created by the rebel bombing. Since the Gamemakers could not easily tell when tributes had passed away, there were no nightly displays of those tributes who had passed away during the day. Additionally, the bodies of dead tributes were not removed by hovercraft, but were instead left in the arena to be dealt with or not dealt with by the remaining tributes as they saw fit. There were no stylists and thus tributes were not dressed in elaborate costumes prior to entering the Games. There were also no escorts. Sponsorship of tributes was available for the first time, though the drone delivery system used to deliver the gifts had not yet been perfected. Though a presenter was tapped to be the first ever host of the Games for a television audience, he only had previous experience reporting the weather and the broadcast thus lacked the polish of latter presentations.','{"source": "10th Hunger Games.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 4, "position": 4, "chunk_index": 4, "total_chunks": 6, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/10th Hunger Games.txt", "parent_document_id": "9b0010b8-1638-440d-8b2f-8f53d65a079f"}','[0.03509474,0.05939601,0.045118734,0.0080602,0.03762174,-0.031218382,0.00081254344,-0.008110336,-0.042347465,0.007690462,-0.05309121,-0.039030056,0.05672898,-0.03404686,-0.026680717,-0.040008783,0.053810604,0.0035036749,-0.009454594,0.062223725,0.00019458956,-0.020298528,0.031379323,-0.096004166,0.024383595,0.0062424205,0.0340802