	 ('b6d7153a-5c44-4e41-844e-308295f88831'::uuid,'Tributes from one district were known for using electrical traps, drones, and reactivated land mines. Tributes from another district were known for weaponizing poison and using the arena''s force field against opponents.
Flight
When faced with a fight they knew they couldn''t win, a tribute could choose to run away.

Resource management
Hunting and foraging
Tributes with some skill and knowledge of hunting, foraging, trapping, or fishing could feed themselves with the arena''s plant and animal life. However, this strategy proved fatal during one The Fire Games because everything in the arena was poisonous.
Salvaging
Tributes sometimes took items that other tributes had discarded, or more frequently, they claimed dead tributes'' possessions as spoils of war. In one The Fire Games, they often took each other''s sponsor gifts; however, this left them susceptible to decoy tactics where the items left behind could actually be harmful.
Sponsors
Tributes could gain access to food and drink, medicine, and weapons by endearing themselves to sponsors during the Games. These people paid for tributes to receive gifts inside the arena, sent by their respective mentors.
Stealing
Tributes have also been known to steal from each other. One tribute maneuvered around a field of land mines to steal from the Careers, taking very little so the items'' absence would not be noticed.','{"source": "Hunger Games tactics.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 2, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Hunger Games tactics.txt", "parent_document_id": "da031f7a-4647-41be-8fc0-294c74bd3fd6"}','[0.031551663,0.073923096,-0.003781918,0.044951867,0.012644423,-0.051869184,0.00294273,-0.036292113,-0.05537987,0.018264461,-0.06945283,-0.02692153,0.023573851,-0.02206017,-0.016797166,-0.031511027,0.027891127,0.022315037,-0.018565273,0.059011836,0.036498263,0.026130175,-0.012688418,-0.05711488,0.011679615,0.009442405,0.11940523,-0.024812616,-0.13962609,-0.03695652,-0.01602188,-0.0056212246,-0.024545155,0.034109354,-0.0044906405,-0.014673729,0.014622389,-0.005248939,0.0070058987,-0.0058371206,0.0021277976,0.008148993,0.008368465,0.02161729,-0.014766303,0.0015114307,0.03082806,-0.022919264,-0.0002755514,-0.010955625,0.044343695,-0.030429682,-0.021020455,0.048099726,0.061640404,-0.003768477,-0.029019717,0.01118939,-0.036308035,0.027020173,0.029605832,0.008667719,0.019563355,0.039200798,0.02849632,-0.026282862,-0.018677525,-0.020188432,-0.023895605,-0.018207945,0.01871773,0.01528049,0.0028074353,0.018170731,0.01563948,-0.035047,-0.06477339,-0.06707853,0.013250956,0.015828775,0.0020807253,-0.029841447,-0.01952068,-0.025912685,0.06179776,-0.009194465,-0.03155088,0.009611744,-0.02462536,0.015391208,-0.06212022,0.012606622,-0.009641176,0.030330822,-0.0008345754,0.00056374224,0.035503753,0.030243732,-0.042276874,0.017318139,-0.029775886,0.038102463,-0.029222697,-0.012851866,0.0077426136,-0.0021194909,-0.007531308,-0.026703145,0.026892135,-0.019001711,-0.0063976087,-0.00450566,0.02687475,0.0060349335,-0.0054884744,-0.03314532,0.017952392,0.011604888,0.017798973,0.06631283,0.02474