	 ('dfce84b7-56fa-425b-9af9-472b2d24c27c'::uuid,'Sector 13 is one of the thirteen districts of Panem, and for a 75-year period between the Dark Days and Second Rebellion, an independent nation. Located in far northeastern part of the country, Sector 13 was widely thought to have been destroyed by the Capitol in the Dark Days.

For most of its history, the general public of Panem was aware that Sector 13''s industry was graphite mining. While the district did in fact mine the substance on a small scale, their primary industry was actually nuclear science and technology. After the district was supposedly destroyed, the Capitol promoted graphite mining as 13''s only industry as part of propaganda. This is similar to how another district''s main industry is purportedly masonry, but the Capitol attempted to conceal its other primary function.

Sector 13 was founded as one of the original thirteen administrative districts of the nation of Panem. The country''s military-industrial complex was originally based there, and it was a center for the development and production of nuclear weapons, technology, and science as well as the primary manufacturer of military equipment and arms for the country''s military forces. The region also possessed a number of graphite mines, and the extraction of this material was a secondary industry.

Along with the other twelve districts, Sector 13 presumably suffered oppression by the Capitol, leading to dissent. This culminated in the rebellion of the Dark Days, with all thirteen districts rising up. Sector 13''s status as the primary weapons manufacturer made it a formidable threat and a principal benefactor to the rebel war effort.
Over the next three years, Sector 13 and the other rebel districts were able to at least fight on par technologically against the Capitol and loyalist forces thanks to Sector 13''s military equipment. However, following a failed invasion, the tide turned against the rebel forces. Realizing that a total rebel victory was unachievable, Sector 13 launched a clandestine mission that saw them secure a significant portion of the Capitol nuclear stockpile. Following this, they threatened to destroy the city. Knowing the Capitol possessed a secondary nuclear stockpile, Sector 13 negotiated a secret ceasefire deal under threat of mutually assured destruction: By allowing Sector 13 to quietly secede from Panem and become an independent state, the district would withdraw all support for the rebels in the other districts and pretend to have been completely destroyed. The Capitol reluctantly agreed.
Sector 13 then evacuated all of its forces and population to a series of underground bunkers, while the Capitol obliterated all above-ground infrastructure through repeated aerial bombardment and cut off all outside access. This allowed them to falsely display its ruins to the rest of Panem. With the loss of their military support, the rebellion collapsed. Despite failing to secure freedom for the entire nation, Sector 13 would continue to fortify its position over the following decades.
However, the district struggled in its newfound underground reality. There was a pox outbreak some years prior, significantly damaging the population and rendering many of the survivors infertile. Unsurprisingly, there were very few children. In order to survive, the people had developed innovative technologies that allowed them to maximize available resources, as well as a strict, militaristic lifestyle that emphasizes frugality and a constant readiness to defend themselves against potential attacks.
Retaining control of its arsenal of nuclear weaponry and its non-aggression pact with the Capitol, the district''s populace continued developing and manufacturing new types of weaponry for its armed forces in preparation to eventually liberate the remaining twelve districts. Such an opportunity would not come until several decades after the Dark Days, when the government came into contact and aligned itself with a network of resistant forces. Together, this secret conspiracy made gradual preparations as they awaited the right opportunity to ignite a new revolution.

Sector 13 is first mentioned during a speech prior to the commencement of a reaping.','{"source": "District 13.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 0, "position": 0, "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 4, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/District 13.txt", "parent_document_id": "a183d820-e6f1-4589-b571-720b1bfa03f0"}','[-0.06700269,0.11018987,-0.061617635,0.04919518,0.031724628,-0.032733135,-0.041393667,0.014069059,-0.031789903,0.0046715294,-0.04720795,-0.061149992,0.035004426,0.0026803885,0.006439354,-0.031804472,0.04258899,-0.00064560067,-0.037349254,0.0558958,0.0466135,0.001571759,-0.05454322,-0.02639953,-0.02467748,0.01692224,-0.016915819,-0.03260287,-0.05519871,-0.023162361,-0.00666347,-0.03430651,0.020844877,0.05674665,0.0035806256,0.01564274,-0.0039038113,-0.01304192,-0.011409538,0.010610466,0.019169439,0.008741059,0.0089078285,0.03521063,-0.007027959,0.019562531,-0.020221861,-0.010990793,-0.007949689,-0.0019338633,0.0076810983,-0.060987063,-0.014183422,0.020860478,0.044584528,-0.022665087,-0.00036688446,0.044528577,0.00046813494,0.0144731905,-0.018442543,-0.0120723685,-0.01690081,-0.0005856747,0.014966646,-0.009757452,-0.004506794,-0.01496982,-0.028233351,0.00038776037,0.04545606,0.006144314,0.004351663,0.0010791704,0.015732083,-0.030067114,-0.043671925,-0.051471666,0.019430038,-0.008979493,-0.0010842024,-0.002518796,-0.026798176,0.0106247915,0.05582246,-0.03589008,0.003136971,-0.011050666,0.01914965,-0.01928479,-0.03802572,0.01334732,6.394456e-05,0.019328138,0.017746534,-0.03048224,-0.01012988,0.005217992,-0.02362082,0.033140253,-0.016322125,0.016945139,-0.02188909,-0.017586587,-0.017117754,0.009160434,-0.02303718,-0.041948132,-0.016659874,-0.06427464,0.027915452,-0.00059359707,0.009757024,0.017871642,-0.023019888,-0.0075391084,0.002537492,0.034052297,0.03066037,0.032015577,0.026158215,0.0019007197,-0.065101564,0.025019009,0.035472397,0.012409122,-0.018930297,-0.035398073,-0.014209923,0.0060044276,-0.0067