	 ('9ee397a4-b3ce-4c0f-83d5-1bf475ff633d'::uuid,'During the speech, the story was told of how the districts of Panem rose, and how Sector 13 was obliterated during the Dark Days. It would later be recalled that graphite mining was an industry in Sector 13 before it was obliterated, and that when the district was occasionally shown on television, it was still smoldering from the toxic bombs dropped on it.

Sector 13 is not mentioned again until an encounter with two refugees from an uprising in another district. The two mentioned they were trying to reach Sector 13, initially causing confusion as to why they would want to go to a place that was nothing but smoldering ruins. The duo proceeded to explain their theory that the destruction story might not be completely true: whenever the Capitol shows television footage of Sector 13, the ruins are indeed always smoldering. While this does tie in with the Capitol''s official position that the area is still uninhabitable, they realized that the exact same mockingjay made an appearance in every broadcast, even in ones supposedly filmed years apart. The two concluded that the Capitol never actually shows the current state of the district, but simply replays old footage.
As such, they believe that the district is still inhabited, with the people living underground. They also express their belief that the Capitol may have in fact left Sector 13 alone in the first place because of the district''s specialty in nuclear weaponry. Following a rescue from a Hunger Games arena, it was learned that not only was Sector 13 still inhabited, but it was being used as the base for a new rebellion.

After a Quarter Quell, several individuals were rescued and brought to Sector 13, along with survivors from the bombing of another district. Upon arrival, a fuller history of the place was learned: Due to the non-aggression pact they established with the Capitol seventy-five years earlier, Sector 13 has remained politically independent and isolated from the rest of Panem. In exchange for this freedom, they promised not to attack the Capitol and start a nuclear war, terms that the Capitol was willing to accept. As a result of their political isolation, Sector 13 has never participated in The Hunger Games.
The individuals subsequently began training for their roles in the Second Rebellion as part of their service for Sector 13''s war machine.
During an interview, a warning was issued on live TV that the Capitol was going to bomb the district. This unexpected warning gave them a ten-minute head start to evacuate the populace to the fortified bunkers in the district''s lower levels.
Sector 13 would go on to play a valuable role in securing freedom for the entire nation throughout the Second Rebellion, through its roles as a weapons supplier and communications center. The district also provided air support to the rebels. Following the victory of the rebellion and the establishment of the Constitutional Republic, Sector 13 was presumably reintegrated into Panem and its above-ground infrastructure rebuilt.

Prior to the Dark Days, Sector 13 was originally one of the thirteen districts of Panem. The governance during this time period is largely unknown.
Following its secession during the Dark Days, Sector 13 became an independent, albeit underground state. It appears to be modelled as a republic, as the district is led by an executive named the President. As Sector 13, alongside the other twelve districts, were fighting for freedom in both wars, it can be assumed that Sector 13 was a democracy, at least in principle. Due to the unique circumstance, however, of the district''s existence and the constant threat posed by the Capitol, the government operated more as a stratocracy, a government ruled by military chiefs. The entire citizen population was drafted into the service or support of the district''s armed forces and the government overall taking on a militaristic form. This lifestyle was borne out of necessity and for the greater benefit of everyone.','{"source": "District 13.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 4, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/District 13.txt", "parent_document_id": "a183d820-e6f1-4589-b571-720b1bfa03f0"}','[-0.04141547,0.117584236,-0.052878987,0.021937843,0.018310772,-0.02452716,-0.026531918,0.013382775,-0.03261111,0.0148225995,-0.037302215,-0.065549366,0.04750727,-0.027088568,0.017213285,-0.010053739,0.03314616,0.029663483,-0.041798983,0.07566987,0.025477242,0.007269263,-0.04216231,-0.063838094,-0.01989029,-0.004386034,-0.0052543855,-0.011694233,-0.06877361,-0.01777952,0.0012854579,-0.027275423,0.013033338,0.058191154,-0.0032513181,0.01889941,-0.018133424,-0.011142458,-0.00802129,0.009357127,0.0027612674,-0.0007410336,0.0031939948,0.03722622,0.013778876,0.010125266,-0.019591965,-0.01013578,-0.01720609,-0.015769582,0.0018606407,-0.065094516,-0.019412939,0.01873701,0.034046248,-0.018343186,0.0076670726,0.05291667,-0.019654792,0.020682622,-0.009278959,-0.011508398,-0.024639392,0.006919912,0.013225235,-0.006237511,0.0036985585,-0.025242362,-0.016979624,-0.015458119,0.04701984,0.009299266