	 ('b9936c9b-2905-441d-8daf-e51f07197a11'::uuid,'Sector 13 is led by a President, who serves as the presumed head of state and government and commander-in-chief of the district''s armed forces. How the President is selected is not specified, although an election of some form is likely. Whether Sector 13 possesses a legislature or a judiciary remains unspecified.

Citizens live a highly regimented life: Every morning, each citizen gets a temporary tattoo on the underside of their arm that shows their daily schedule. The schedule displays, in 24-hour time, where to be and what activities are to be performed at specific times. After a certain time, the ink breaks down and can be washed off in preparation for the following day.
Activities such as meals - which are normally taken communally - are scheduled regularly every day and participated in by all citizens. Other activities can vary significantly and depend on several factors: Children under the age of 14 attend school. Depending on their background, children may have other duties in addition to schooling. If you are over 14, you qualify for the rank of "soldier" and receive military training in addition to some educational sessions. Activities for adults appear to be more specialized. At some point during the day, citizens are given 30 minutes of downtime with family.
Although schedules are not usually subject to change, special conditions could be negotiated.

Weddings are relatively low-key events; the couple signs a marriage certificate and they''re assigned a compartment to share. Due to their strict, frugal lifestyle, the citizens are not much prone to celebration, and it seems they have no holidays at all.

Sector 13 was the primary weapons supplier. This made them a formidable threat to the Capitol''s power when war broke out. Its military might and arsenal played a crucial role in the Dark Days and the Second Rebellion, making the other districts'' armed insurrections possible. The district''s other primary industry, nuclear weapons development and research, also saw it producing a significant stockpile of nuclear missiles. These weapons of mass destruction would be instrumental in allowing it to propose the ceasefire permitting its independence in the first place.
During its 75 years as an independent nation, Sector 13 continued building upon its armed forces, developing special weaponry and new military technology. In addition to its seized pile of nuclear weapons, Sector 13 also possessed a fleet of hovercraft, with some of it formerly belonging to the Capitol''s Peacekeeping Force. Notably, however, Sector 13''s hovercraft appear to be less sophisticated than the Capitol-derived variants.
All able-bodied citizens aged fourteen years and above are obliged to serve in the armed forces.

According to a map, Sector 13 is located in the northeast of Panem. Its territory is primarily centered around a region. This location ties into its secondary industry of graphite mining, as notable sources of graphite are located there. Similarly, in the region that Sector 13 occupies, historically there were nuclear reactors and supplementary nuclear research and technology facilities.
Sector 13 borders three other districts.
Before the end of the Dark Days, Sector 13 existed on the surface like all of the other districts. It is unknown whether the district was affluent or poor, although given its district industry and its status as the then center of the military-industrial complex, the former is highly likely. The district was likely more urbanized than rural.
Following its independence, the entirety of the District''s surface infrastructure was leveled by a series of intense bombing raids as stipulated in the ceasefire deal. The district in turn relocated its populace, industry, and military to a vast series of underground bunkers. When these bunkers were constructed and their extent is unknown. Similarly, it is unknown if Sector 13 comprises just a singular massive bunker or a large central bunker with a number of smaller satellite bunkers throughout the district.','{"source": "District 13.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 2, "position": 2, "chunk_index": 2, "total_chunks": 4, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/District 13.txt", "parent_document_id": "a183d820-e6f1-4589-b571-720b1bfa03f0"}','[-0.010090738,0.10109764,-0.036198586,0.024801906,0.0030636443,-0.005461371,-0.006595035,-0.0042141587,-0.010808439,-0.006981546,-0.044576615,-0.031287443,0.0948052,-0.003974718,0.020988047,0.005824228,-0.020853987,-0.014591274,-0.021677736,0.057081543,0.012231858,0.016123625,-0.007426083,-0.048053857,0.004403959,0.023004465,0.023596933,0.0031871533,-0.06297499,-0.034571227,-0.002320488,-0.039039392,-0.0071586343,0.07878296,-0.041125827,0.005307858,-0.0077180685,-0.022690058,-0.011965893,0.0136506185,-0.0115926815,0.029390553,-0.00067099836,0.042983912,0.0063615204,0.0017770692,-0.024341622,0.0066043683,-0.0123716155,0.006169949,0.008974421,-0.064210035,-0.004283603,0.012511812,0.018559398,-0.011858911,0.021038858,0.025729287,-0.0108131,0.009395899,-0.011307093,-0.05061567,-0.032393586,-0.0031783713,0.0015168602,-0.012369859,0.00025034364,-0.035122413,-0.0315606,-0.00076866813,0.04228174,0.006420375,-0.0044860253,0.032670002,0.010977864,0.008737309,-0.04519087,-0.02329342,-0.0040671974,0.0063352957,-0.025092883,-0.006510883,-0.051333528,-0.015458761,0.04613894,-0.04548602,-0.010047455,-0.014756013,-0.0025819868,-0.02749039,-0.038745973,0.015962206,-0.0041094073,0.02776557,0.01