	 ('dac9e60d-a752-4318-a6bb-b67fc819ec41'::uuid,'What is known, however, is that the underground bunkers were both large and sophisticated enough to be self-sustaining for a population estimated to be numbering in the few ten of thousands for three-quarters of a century with no outside help. Sector 13 was even able to take on survivors from another district with little to no difficulty. Additionally, the bunkers housed a vast quantity of military equipment, weapons, vehicles, and supplies along with factories for continual production. The bunkers were fortified enough to withstand significant attacks, with only the top layers of the underground complex damaged or destroyed by bunker-buster missiles during an attack in the Second Rebellion.

Sector 13 is the only district to never take part in a Hunger Games event.
It and one other are the only districts with dual industries, though no other district knew about its second primary industry. However, nuclear energy and graphite mining are closely related, as graphite is one of the most important components of a nuclear reactor.
In its prime, Sector 13 may have been one of the larger districts: One reason the destruction story was doubted was that the mines themselves were small and few in number, and the population of 13 was known to be much larger than what small scale mining actually required.
Sector 13 is the only known district to be located underground, though it originally existed above ground before the Dark Days.
Sector 13 is one of the three known districts to be bombed during the Second Rebellion.
There was an epidemic a few years prior that caused significant population loss.
Due to Sector 13 not participating in the Hunger Games, no official arena wear for Sector 13 was produced. Because of this, it is difficult to determine what the district''s color could be. However, considering the district''s dual industries before the Dark Days and the district''s evolution into a military-centric nation, the district''s color seems to be dark silver gray.','{"source": "District 13.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 3, "position": 3, "chunk_index": 3, "total_chunks": 4, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/District 13.txt", "parent_document_id": "a183d820-e6f1-4589-b571-720b1bfa03f0"}','[-0.020934464,0.1013174,-0.04917834,0.057386015,0.013183865,-0.013260559,-0.012360799,-0.009372789,-0.014624155,0.017153844,-0.019630486,-0.028106017,0.023118699,0.04316994,0.026233632,-0.0037419116,0.008137298,0.008274653,-0.04267913,0.086534955,0.06138626,-0.025587294,-0.05151637,-0.0202177,-0.014093844,0.044113778,-0.02706111,-0.0277975,-0.061880894,-0.045140963,-0.0017721287,-0.004265957,0.019539448,0.028850485,-0.0025192033,0.0021813775,-0.021520153,-0.027938817,0.0046792338,0.024059149,0.014803547,-0.0057522384,0.000767341,0.01484616,0.005008754,0.014343707,-0.012816618,-0.014380236,-0.017727086,0.0047528856,0.02402378,-0.044061936,-0.016622836,0.035392847,0.04149345,-0.038657926,-0.006405896,0.02199919,-0.020523105,0.002818202,-0.019387977,-0.026175413,-0.012916889,0.0069475323,0.015637236,-0.0034219949,0.0020682376,-0.011473216,-0.014608716,0.0047951224,0.047291417,0.025630228,0.0015946353,-0.006044739,0.009189906,-0.024561489,-0.04853379,-0.037895784,0.0133519815,-0.0066166907,-0.013501346,-0.030297931,-0.059463654,0.0065969485,0.033578575,-0.033579197,-0.0037452905,-0.010285832,-0.0016950073,-0.02069596,-0.04464951,0.015752336,-0.01086619,0.026879586,0.00027225204,-0.0014390423,0.004876307,0.010341486,-0.0316917,0.051183786,0.0034496337,0.031479925,-0.051511295,-0.023891658,-0.0033002386,-0.01336053,-0