	 ('2430abc5-ed18-499b-aa48-43406d0c79a8'::uuid,'Each of the contestants were given an interview.

One tribute was described as very beautiful. It was noted that her mentor probably didn''t have much trouble thinking of an angle of approach to make herself seem a good bet.
Another showed confidence and made jokes during the interview.
Another was arrogant and ready. She confirmed high skills with knives.
Another was noted as a monstrous, ruthless killing-machine. He said he was determined to win.
Another''s interview was said to be nothing special.
Another was sly and elusive. She spoke very little but when she did it was noted that she was quiet. In one adaptation, it was shown that she talked fast and used many intelligent words.
Another was very quiet and shy.
Another was not very shy, saying the best strategy is speed, saying that if they can''t be caught, they can''t be killed. She was dressed in a gossamer gown complete with wings making the audience in awe.
Another was very large, and attempted to answer the questions with single yes or no answers. It was thought that if there was any money, it would be bet on this tribute.

One tribute was very nervous and couldn''t think straight during the interview. Her stylist told her to be honest and pretend like the interview questions are coming from a familiar person to calm her down and throughout the interview, she reminded herself to be honest. She won over the audience by showing off her outfit and twirling around, making her look beautiful. She said that her favorite thing was a certain food and that she would be trying to win for a family member. She had a dress in which the bottom was fabricated and made her look like she was on fire when she twirled. When asked about an unusually high training score, she was vague on the details, saying only that what she did was a first.

Another tribute won over the audience with looks and sense of humor. He joked and asked the host if he smelled like roses. He makes a joke about the showers, and the host states that he is charming and has a wonderful sense of humor. He also revealed that he has had a crush on his female counterpart for a long time, which started a story about star crossed lovers.

Only some of the tributes have interview scenes in one adaptation. But some of the interviews were cut. Some did not have interview scenes, but were shown in a queue scene.
Some were completely omitted in the adaptation''s interview and lineup scenes.

Both appear for the post-Games interview. One is told that they must act as though they are madly in love and that she would rather have died than to lose the other. Due to a defiant act, the leadership is not very happy with them. Their stylists, prep teams, escort and mentor are all introduced. One is dressed as an innocent young girl in a dress that resembled candlelight to draw attention away from rebellious actions. They show highlights and it is especially hard to re-live. When the crown is given, a venomous look is given and it is known that revenge will be had.

To wrap up a Triumphal Journey, there is an interview. During, he asks how the victor is doing. During one interview, a proposal is made. This was an idea and was the signal for a planned uprising.

Each victor reaped participated in an interview, a process not new to any of them. Most complained or showed sadness of the fact that they would have to participate in yet another games, while some, mainly the careers, boasted of their fame or showed the same bloodlust as before.

One makes a speech about how she could not stop crying when she thinks of how the residents must be suffering with the thought of the loss. In an adaptation, both siblings go up at the same time. During the interview, it is stated that both turned the event into a family affair. One speaks after the other does.','{"source": "Interviews.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 3, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Interviews.txt", "parent_document_id": "a2c6f42e-fd57-44a1-a58f-f3e6f976e877"}','[0.042934094,0.03789416,0.032597378,-0.017208617,0.009848304,-0.05857687,0.03703703,0.017126717,0.006323048,0.026645718,-0.027079716,-0.013884274,0.05842138,-0.010015114,-0.042141598,-0.009667697,-0.00093080936,0.034033965,-0.0011917419,0.043721553,-0.042337444,0.05428207,0.00636593,-0.08138979,-0.017750494,-0.002060919,0.046436705,0.018397821,-0.099402785,0.03026986,0.037378505,0.031335983,-0.013827517,0.00277599,-0.02156978,0.03713674,0.019372493,-0.039241683,0.011198001,-0.022229264,-0.026927603,0.033487834,-0.008201331,0.022674475,0.015737008,0.0090943985,0.02645485,-0.024748713,-0.025963362,0.00683902,0.03834821,-0.03582006,-0.010418432,-0.009839973,0.008616024,0.0030750837,0.004216109,0.0033822546,-0.047200564,-0.012305131,-0.019741487,0.0059197266,0.03240379,0.054722983,0.020419583,-0.027309895,-0.011507021,0.0020741737,-0.0109486915,0.033137098,0.035608277,-0.0012186189,0.020822164,0.03130041,0.02756598,-0.07352266,-0.06812829,-0.034071475,-0.012936694,0.036807917,0.0050351773,-0.007909717,-0.030101376,-0.02569325,0.013264298,-0.03712266,0.0128197195,0.012341997,-0.02513489,0.0014797918,-0.03816877,0.018200452,-0.0018859253,0.035642482,-0.0124302255,0.012899822,0.0018257893,-0.0048413277,-0.04029392,-0.0039533176,-0.012828605,0.029664407,-0.0014336064,-0.021632554,-0.0016039822,-0.023944074,0.004270071,-0.047149524,0.02510783,-0.0061982353,-0.0652415,0.013544159,0.02485