	 ('29ab8692-acc5-469c-a4a9-96adf26e0764'::uuid,'In rage at his death, the other tribute dropped his spear and took his ax, which he used for the rest of the Games, and chopped down part of the arena.

He was noted as being barely five feet tall. His voice hadn''t been changed by puberty yet. Alongside the rest of the District 7 tributes, he wore electric blue in the arena.

He was a very kind and smart boy, coming up with the idea of a huge alliance to possibly counter the careers. He was friendly to everyone but builds a specific bond with another tribute. His father agreed that he was a "great kid".

He first met another tribute during a training session for the 50th Hunger Games where he took a liking to that tribute for mocking the president on another tribute''s death. He and that tribute developed a friendship where the latter decided to join an alliance formed by him against the Careers. When that tribute found out he was a victor''s son and was reaped in order to punish his father for his rebellious activities, that tribute promised his father he would look after him as they worked to blow up the arena.

During the Games, he and that tribute teamed up to carry out their plan to destroy the arena''s water tank. However, their attempt only partially damaged the arena and the Gamemakers retaliated by sending squirrel mutts programmed to attack only him as punishment for his rebelliousness. That tribute tried to save him, but was unable to get the mutts away from his friend. In rage and sadness over his death, that tribute chopped down part of the arena in his grief and took his ax, which he used for the rest of the Games.','{"source": "Ampert Latier.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 2, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Ampert Latier.txt", "parent_document_id": "0cbbc6ff-8c27-4c09-a8bd-0c55f56ce711"}','[0.08649565,0.098831326,0.031426653,1.7980116e-06,-0.038868845,-0.047169726,0.014504099,-0.013768767,-0.023192137,0.024548158,-0.06846938,-0.050599687,0.03421396,-0.04121534,-0.053332202,-0.03936334,0.044926573,0.06098875,-0.01908524,0.05682424,-0.00803318,0.009367275,0.007991701,-0.07763281,0.015756302,0.015363122,0.0072860382,-0.013646889,-0.10765198,-0.021803295,0.0104858,-0.0049925474,-0.017127682,0.031651042,-0.01123294,0.034892257,0.029384049,0.0040271142,0.004082899,-0.018215204,0.03094731,-0.00242001,0.0028584104,0.015676565,0.0038809297,0.022645159,0.013979061,-0.018803172,-0.0047491165,-0.019516345,0.026504537,-0.042931605,-0.02365603,0.03884118,0.035814613,-0.0031154496,-0.011198907,0.01845791,-0.027401427,0.017571462,0.0005459799,0.01785921,-0.0020273188,0.003493271,0.006255863,-0.030025803,-0.03245316,-0.014079353,0.0024727003,0.017159458,0.049203433,0.011804914,0.012845744,0.011118074,0.022274375,-0.050781433,-0.06400025,-0.06242379,0.0010527832,-0.0020003533,0.026102286,-0.03298765,-0.044832468,-0.031106241,0.026941884,-0.03212112,-0.022305533,0.009886713,0.0013317835,0.016770408,-0.015925743,-0.004746972,0.003410336,0.019054161,0.008084694,-0.02906