	 ('78bcbe57-56e8-41e7-9be5-800a21e722c1'::uuid,'In theory, most knives can be used as throwing weapons, but some are specifically designed for the purpose.

A mace consists of a length of shaft topped by a heavy weight. Historically, there have been many variations of this weapon; some heads may be spiked or have angular striking surfaces, and others may place the weight at the end of a chain, which in turn is connected to the shaft. A bar mace is a narrow pole weapon consisting of a hand grip attached to two flattened metal bars intersecting at the middle, giving the weapon a "+"-shaped cross section. It is a simple but efficient weapon that can be used to bludgeon and hit opponents.

A machete is a type of heavy, long-bladed knife which can be used as an agricultural tool and as a weapon.

A net is composed of fibers woven in a grid-like structure. It blocks the passage of large items, while letting smaller items and fluids pass. It requires less material than something sheet-like, and provides a degree of transparency. Nets can be used to catch fish, birds, animals, or for ensnaring people.

A pickaxe is a mining tool that has a sharp metal spike on each side of its long handle. It is typically used for prying, but has also been adapted for warfare.

A pitchfork is an agricultural tool with a long handle and metal prongs fixed to one end.

Poison is a deadly substance that can kill anything that ingests it.

A scalpel chain is a weapon that almost looks like a metal rope with multiple spikes consisting further down the rope.

A sickle is an agricultural tool that is traditionally used for harvesting crops, but could also be used as a weapon. Typically, they consist of a short handle connected to a curved or crescent moon-shaped blade, and are used for slashing and cutting.

A slingshot is a projectile weapon that can be used to fling small objects such as stones at short distances.

A snare is a rope or wire that is tied to an object to trap prey and kill it.

A spear is a pole weapon consisting of a long shaft and a pointed head. Depending on the time period and culture, the head could take many different designs and be made from a variety of materials; the end of the shaft may simply be sharpened, or the head may be a separate piece made of more durable material and attached to the shaft. Spears are one of the few weapons that are always supplied at the Cornucopia.

The sunflower bomb was an explosive specifically designed to be safe, both chemically and structurally and couldn''t be set off unintentionally by the user or anything else. They could only be detonated by being fully assembled and the fuse lit with fire.

A sword consists of hand grip, or hilt, attached to a blade. Depending on the design of the sword, it may be used primarily for cutting and/or thrusting, and the blade may have one or two edges. A serrated sword consists of a short hand grip attached to the blade. One side is smooth and sharp while the other is serrated and pointed.

A trident is a three-pronged spear that can be used both as a weapon and for spear fishing. In addition to stabbing, the prongs on a trident can be used to trap other weapons and deflect them away from the wielder.

A baton is a long, narrow rod that can be made from many different materials. As a weapon, a baton may be used to strike, jab, block, bludgeon, and aid in the application of armlocks.

The Capitol was known to carpet bomb rebellious districts into submission.

Traps devised by Gamemakers, typically for use in a Hunger Games arena. During one Games, a massive wall of fire was unleashed to force the tributes closer together in the arena. Fireballs were also shot at the tributes.','{"source": "Weapons.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 3, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Weapons.txt", "parent_document_id": "2386de9d-e756-49ae-a960-6b6307ef44c2"}','[0.034744665,0.037811663,0.03311607,0.08077225,-0.02587316,-0.04244079,0.027988568,-0.029038757,-0.048305634,-0.00940556,-0.09552086,-0.0018652064,0.030882616,-0.02368214,0.022230664,-0.010797822,0.04106928,0.008870633,-0.002181174,0.076541245,0.033541773,0.022628417,0.057860583,0.00050431874,-0.0013656048,0.06110323,0.024440572,-0.060787532,-0.09341474,-0.07681173,-0.007977785,-0.027344944,-0.0003010159,0.050668336,-0.040583,-0.009693642,-0.019703723,0.008534907,0.011677666,-0.03298057,-0.025944235,-0.0069848155,0.023527468,0.004029276,0.00309274,-0.00058882474,0.022362564,-0.0032378086,-0.0064922487,0.016623393,0.021666257,-0.04469243,0.021930434,0.019740477,0.032530714,0.016656091,-0.0213712,-0.0071050315,-0.04913539,0.004778113,0.014558586,0.003004378,-0.0067697307,0.031356327,-0.010708347,-0.01480561,-0.0059764157,-0.049573623,0.024846606,0.023455169,-0.026490822,-0.053921446,0.012661157,0.0067672404,0.049093544,0.007611091,-0.058980893,-0.044555787,0.024130011,-0.015916783,-0.015801672,-0.014702508,-0.058384817,0.020022115,0.05934304,-0.005597113,-0.007652891,0.010858134,-0.029964224,0.021639422,-0.027657919,-0.008731712,-0.025629234,0.02992819,-0.03172118,-0.04437963,0.036330286,-0.007022581,-0.0338547,0.021570686,-0.025678309,0.036240675,-0.009832248,-0.027293917,-0.0013165134,-0.0068343063,-0.02499253,-0.027370747,0.012473973,0.0017822911,-0.001932832,0.00667785,0.020349396,-0.014503202,-0.02265993,-0.01034661,-0.025417162,0.021644777,0.047230747,0.037510093,0.0342