	 ('3ed489f1-ac91-4460-b1dc-a3434e12001a'::uuid,'During another Games, one of the hourly obstacles encountered in the arena was a poisonous fog. Any skin that came in contact with the mist instantly erupted in extremely painful swellings, and too long or too heavy exposure resulted in death. Submersion in water helped to dull the pain and draw out the poison. Gamemakers genetically engineered many twisted creatures to set upon tributes in the arena.

In this setting, guns are only authorized for use by Sentinel Corps. The standard rifle could fire a hundred rounds before reloading. Other guns could convert solar energy into deadly rays of power, eliminating the need for ammunition.

Pods are Gamemaker-designed obstacles deployed throughout the city to kill invading rebels.

A water cannon is a device that shoots a high-pressure stream of water. Typically, a water cannon can deliver a large volume of water, often over hundreds of feet. They are used in firefighting and riot control.

A whip is a weapon, mostly used for punishment but also for combat. It is used by "cracking" the whip through the air, making it hit an opponent painfully. Whips also typically feature a hard butt that can be used as a bludgeon.

Having gained political independence from the Capitol, one district had its own supply of guns, which they distributed to rebel forces across all districts during rebellions. Rebels bombed strategic locations. In one district, there was an entire wall of archery weapons. In particular, a militarized bow was weighed down with scopes and gadgetry. Simulated Street Combat training involved the possibility of triggering a mine in preparation for an assault. During a rebellion, soldiers from one district were given suicide pills to swallow in the event that they were captured. One squad was a sharpshooter unit created to film propaganda for the war effort. As a result, some members used special signature weapons alongside or in place of their standard-issue firearms. A special bow was programmed to only recognize one user''s voice. It was designed with a variety of color-coded arrows to go along with it as well: razor sharp, incendiary, and explosive. A special trident was also made with its own special features. One feature allowed it to be called back to the wielder after it had been thrown.','{"source": "Weapons.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 2, "position": 2, "chunk_index": 2, "total_chunks": 3, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Weapons.txt", "parent_document_id": "2386de9d-e756-49ae-a960-6b6307ef44c2"}','[-0.032037966,0.06516566,0.033849258,0.07482645,0.002108659,-0.050481156,-0.022798851,-0.021907393,-0.022815265,0.018703403,-0.07355045,-0.037903186,0.0771492,0.0051016454,0.029884212,-0.0145350685,0.04688065,0.06798225,-0.028082846,0.06519526,0.057032388,-0.020001607,-0.018373005,-0.044083957,0.024787335,0.06582566,0.018534867,-0.04591651,-0.10062072,-0.073968925,-0.0018142699,-0.013385058,-0.00015445484,0.04049359,-0.059458293,0.004428754,-0.0048727077,0.020491267,-0.006259932,-0.0463255,0.025446035,0.012612143,0.008501109,-0.0052180253,-0.0010035854,0.0049004694,0.011914427,0.0061231935,0.015324561,0.00