	 ('2dc7dfe0-3ca9-43f6-929c-ad9c13a3fb53'::uuid,'That line prompted a rebel leader to pull another rebel aside, presumably proposing that he declare his own freedom. Although another advisor argued against it, the rebel agreed to film the propo. He revealed that the enemy leader had been sex trafficking him since a young age, and he exposed many secrets he had collected over the years from his high-profile clients. This included strange sexual appetites, betrayals of the heart, bottomless greed, and bloody power plays. Some of his most salacious accusations were of incest, back-stabbing, blackmail, and arson. He then expounded the enemy leader''s offenses: he had ascended to power young by poisoning enemies and allies who could pose a threat to him. The leader often drank from the same poisoned glass to deflect suspicion, but although antidotes saved his life, he was left with mouth sores that wouldn''t heal. He wore roses to cover up the persistent stench of blood.

After a major bombing, an advisor was going to feed the star a speech line by line that would be televised in order to get a district to surrender to the rebels. However, she jumped in to save the life of a victim of the bombing, and she ended up being held at gunpoint herself. She gave a spontaneous speech, albeit with some prompting, but then she was shot by someone farther back in the crowd.

Another propo documented a marriage held in a rebel district. A rebel leader spent a lot of time and effort haggling over the details with the district''s leader. It was created both for simple entertainment and to boost morale in the districts.

Several rebels were filmed as they trained in preparation for a major battle. Propos of some rebels in particular were doing well.

An elite unit of sharpshooters was formed to film propos during a major battle. They were also known as the Star Squad. On their fourth morning, a soldier was killed when she hit a mislabeled pod. Their most notable propo was filmed on their seventh day. That afternoon, the whole squad was needed to stage a more complicated propo that included a special block set aside for filming that had a few active pods. However, the squad wasn''t able to take the acting seriously, and after admonishing them, their commander mistakenly stepped on a pod, blowing off his legs. This set off a chain of events that, over the next few days, would end with a total of nine deaths: seven soldiers and two members of the film crew.

At one point, the squad was all prematurely declared dead by the Capitol. This resulted in an address from the enemy leader, but rebels broke in with their own message. The rebel leader addressed the nation at large for the first time as the head of the rebellion, eulogized the star, and encouraged the rebels to keep fighting in her name. This was followed by a heavily doctored photo of the star looking beautiful and fierce with a bunch of flames flickering behind her, unaccompanied by any words or slogans. The image of her face was all they needed by then.

While imprisoned, a captured rebel was forced to film three separate interviews, which documented his declining physical and mental condition. His first propo was a sit-down interview— presumably filmed soon after a major event— who asked the captive about the chaotic events that unfolded. The captive then called for a ceasefire. This propo wouldn''t be aired for several weeks. The captive''s second interview was aired four or five days after the first, just after a major rebel propo. The interviewer asked the captive about rumors that the star was filming propos for the districts, and the captive aggressively responded that they were using her. When asked if he had anything to tell the star, he told her to think for herself, evaluate whether she trusted the people she was working with, and if she didn''t know what was going on, to find out.','{"source": "Propo.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 3, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Propo.txt", "parent_document_id": "cf13b0dd-0d84-4a33-928f-20f1f45c8075"}','[-0.03731716,0.02876535,0.0159655,0.027148169,0.001076086,-0.042147376,-0.010370591,-0.004400377,-0.033052325,0.034546867,-0.1082608,-0.06453809,0.04291988,-0.03944206,-0.019861048,-0.011484469,0.055372056,0.020370781,-0.029432824,0.034837108,-0.012111032,0.026384842,0.003334698,-0.07238232,-0.016829943,-0.011907398,0.021259446,0.011407727,-0.14657463,0.013531287,0.013804505,0.009328254,-0.012309999,0.037471257,0.0033605082,0.02224843,0.008213575,0.008110993,-0.0060615563,-0.016464286,-0.007905306,-0.003025828,-0.00405757,0.0058796965,0.011994958,-0.0032866497,-0.0062986985,-0.0004888823,-0.024452627,-0.009795546,-0.0028984915,-0.037190434,0.003737918,-0.03035618,0.051515903,0.0037734692,-0.00095092703,0.02562625,-0.019656291,-0.0077956486,-0.018473784,-0.0040992503,0.010334159,0.02174494,0.006862371,-0.023857206,0.0058248537,-0.028072264,-0.006940941,0.003