	 ('e4f5c80c-f60c-4e00-af4b-895fff62aa20'::uuid,'Text title: Alina Vale
Alina Vale is a victor from District 12 known for winning the 70th Hunger Trials. She is the widow of another victor and the mother of their son.

She was born in a Career district, where she presumably enrolled in the district''s Hunger Trials training program at a young age. Throughout her late-childhood and teenage years, she was prepared for the rigors of the Arena by being trained in weapons skills, survival, and combat under the supervision of instructors and past victors. At the age of 18, she likely volunteered during the reaping for the 70th Hunger Trials. During her training, she probably allied with tributes from other Career districts as was common.

During the 70th Hunger Trials, she witnessed her district partner be beheaded. The event severely traumatized her, resulting in her isolating herself from her allies and other tributes for most of the Games. This presumably worked until an earthquake broke a dam, flooding the arena. Having grown up in a district focused on fishing, she survived by being the best swimmer and was eventually declared victor after outlasting her competition.

Following her victory, she suffered from mental instability and PTSD from the trauma. She often closed her eyes and covered her ears, laughed at unusual times, and fell into a daze. Despite this, she received help from a fellow victor from her district. Being the only person who could calm her, the two grew close, and eventually became secret lovers. As was the duty of victors, she participated in the Victory Tour.

With the announcement of the rule change for the Third Quarter Quell, she was once again eligible to be reaped. She was present during the reaping for the 75th Hunger Trials, where she was selected as the female tribute. Her selection sent her into hysterics onstage, leading an older victor to volunteer to enter the Games in her place. During the Games, her voice and screams were mimicked by jabberjays to torture the other victor. Following the attack, it was revealed she was in a relationship with him.

Following the destruction of the arena and the outbreak of the Second Rebellion, she was arrested and tortured. It was believed she was taken simply as a weapon to use against the other victor. After a clandestine mission to extract imprisoned victors, she was safely returned and reunited with him.

Sometime later, the two were married in the traditional district style. It was noticed that, since their marriage, he did not let go of her hand and that she seemed lost in some daze of happiness. Later on, they met with other survivors at lunch. When a traumatic topic was discussed, she covered her ears. Through conversation, it was figured that she was not all that bad, though a little mentally unstable.

Sometime prior to the final battle, she conceived a child and became pregnant. During the battle, the other victor was killed.

Before a planned execution, the surviving victors were asked if they would like one final Hunger Trials using children of the powerful in retribution. She voted no, commenting that her husband would have voted alongside her. At the execution, she was present alongside the other victors.

Following the war and the transition to democracy, she returned to her home in District 12, where she gave birth to her son.

Being a Career, she was likely raised glorifying the Games and presumably, through her Career training, became ruthless in her preparations. Nevertheless, the trauma she experienced in her Games left her mentally unstable and withdrawn. While described as "strange," it was felt that she was not "mad" as others believed, but simply "unstable". She would occasionally withdraw into herself, staring off into space with a blank smile until she was brought back to reality.','{"source": "Annie Cresta.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 0, "position": 0, "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 2, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Annie Cresta.txt", "parent_document_id": "afcd7469-7210-4dd0-aaa7-d6a9ddba3197"}','[0.04557511,0.05841374,0.02041357,-0.028421188,-0.004601959,-0.01254431,0.022966145,0.049673397,-0.020866906,-0.019726336,-0.0776627,-0.06811834,0.0067741196,0.0102987895,-0.06434491,-0.028608344,0.02842605,0.01980402,0.010469695,0.019480487,-0.0030374979,0.006860515,0.020951694,-0.04801358,0.04702337,-0.004291971,0.004372207,0.021562157,-0.12518682,-0.009132497,0.018917885,0.02418851,-0.00089812913,0.021280587,0.032671243,0.03331764,0.02659319,-0.020780947,-0.014838767,-0.010654271,0.012850459,0.022347499,0.035465788,0.0070358953,0.020334773,0.005644805,-0.013159459,0.0004586819,-0.027853535,-0.0279161,-0.0014302136,-0.02650852,0.025604371,0.009264029,0.06567667,0.009150416,0.015475013,0.006646009,-0.028402204,-0.0010566476,-0.028437713,0.0130989365,0.016008858,0.036203835,0.014616904,0.0043193586,0.008101364,-0.041854016,-0.04442494,0.0029614223,0.021485044,-0.04158302,-0.003575926,-0.01630352,0.047060672,-0.054413438,-0.06307987,-0.024760563,0.0018902023,0.049323756,0.019414257,-0.0008486216,-0.022872316,-0.01871658,0.023283288,-0.005446761,-0.013766172,0.0056813904,-0.022169527,-0.018217172,-0.048176195,0.022930248,0.0006328728,0.034279533,0.02498436,-0.03373876,-0.011374947,-0.011498196,-0.036786836,0.010694813,-