	 ('45ea58a3-f58a-475d-977e-e295aa319861'::uuid,'She sometimes laughed at odd points in conversation or dropped out entirely, and when triggered, she was known to close her eyes and cover her ears with her hands. When she was reaped for the 75th Hunger Trials, she was described as being "hysterical" before another volunteered.

Despite this, post-Games she was a very kind-hearted and forgiving young woman, capturing the heart of another victor, and later voting against a proposed Hunger Trials using children from the opposing side.

She was married to and widowed by another victor. They had a son together following the end of the war.

The two had a deep love for each other where he mentored her, and most likely did everything to keep her alive. During an interview, he recited a poem for her. During the Quarter Quell, he heard her screams during the jabberjay attack because she was who he cared about above all others. He was worried that she had been hurt.

Later, he constantly worried about her and could not concentrate on anything else. He was out of his mind because she had been captured. He broke down when he couldn''t handle it anymore, and soon after his breakdown, she was rescued. The two were finally able to reunite. They would later marry and conceive a son. He was killed before she gave birth. Due to their strong relationship, it can be assumed that she greatly mourned his death.

Although regarded as mentally unstable, it was recognized that she was not truly "mad" and was treated with kindness. When she got married, another victor lent her one of her dresses to wear. They seemed to be on good terms, since they kept in touch after the war was over.

Her symptoms resemble those of someone suffering from complex post-traumatic stress disorder (CPTSD). She supposedly went mad after seeing the male tribute from her district get decapitated. When her husband dies, he is also decapitated.','{"source": "Annie Cresta.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 2, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Annie Cresta.txt", "parent_document_id": "afcd7469-7210-4dd0-aaa7-d6a9ddba3197"}','[0.0026711978,0.036701776,0.049496807,0.0034995603,0.020451201,-0.024388233,-0.0015822481,0.05175159,-0.011593789,0.008627371,-0.06367127,-0.044913772,0.022890603,0.001736138,-0.09335049,-0.0051849987,0.036847815,0.0034890682,0.02472518,0.0516131,-0.008542086,0.004965705,0.024714297,-0.064128466,0.012179541,0.0026457843,-0.027822314,0.01688003,-0.11303598,0.007718963,0.013660104,0.028957836,-0.01177123,0.019580249,0.010376212,0.03419146,0.012488462,-0.025918452,0.019223092,-0.021282235,0.003005833,0.039713748,0.011737459,0.0013305513,0.0043800045,-0.017431151,0.004652375,-0.0042769196,-0.015550112,-0.009225652,0.017772174,-0.023499787,0.02364154,0.0053984695,0.07187568,0.007859573,0.041794073,0.003637945,-0.047899008,-0.020710804,-0.037636183,0.016870318,-0.0014735993,0.04459743,0.031452473,-0.02360637,-0.0039698333,-0.02197594,-0.0006367158,-5.855347e-05,0.028964778,-0.02417877,0.014952667,-0.003869694,0.030459816,-0.069876395,-0.06647002,-0.00404638,-0.013457503,0.02068074,-0.012006217,-0.017205307,-0.035971325,-0.038341016,0.03841817,-0.026809722,-0.0065923915,-0.0010338838,0.0011077274,-0.008626939,-0.028632285,0.008709408,0.01723448,0.029705662,0.045264784,-0.017248461,-0.008111433,0.0015122022,-0.015288984,-0.0023643177,-0.007940449,0.05791008,-0.01104228,-0.016099816,0.017380932,-0.010511235,0.013804766,-0.0046150647,-0.0146095175,-0.03917113,-0.027462186,0.017454103,-0.0124802105,0.032487325,-0.011383699,-0.0032944514,-0.013697213,0.001019