	 ('a5678d8f-be9c-40d1-82e5-99be59c21b89'::uuid,'This loss presumably has a devastating impact on the rebel war effort, turning the tide of the war in favor of the Capitol.
Realizing that the rebels have lost their advantage, Sector 13 decides to abandon its allies and secure its own independence. They seize a significant portion of the Capitol''s nuclear arsenal and target the city. Knowing the Capitol still has its own nuclear weapons, Sector 13 threatens mutually assured destruction unless the Capitol strikes a deal.
Sector 13''s leaders propose that the Capitol allow them to quietly secede as an independent state, in exchange for their withdrawal of support from the rebel war effort and presenting the illusion that the Capitol destroyed the sector. Left with no other viable alternative and unwilling to elevate the rebellion into a nuclear war, the Capitol reluctantly agrees to the terms of the ceasefire.
Sector 13 consolidates its people and assets in an underground complex, and the Capitol carpet bombs its surface infrastructure.
The Capitol uses the decimated ruins of 13 as propaganda, making an example of it as the consequence for rebelling. With the loss of support from Sector 13, the rebellion collapses and is overrun by the Capitol. The remaining districts are pacified and reunified under the firm grip of the Capitol.

The Hunger Trials Era (0 ADD - 74 ADD)
After the districts'' defeat and the end of the Dark Days, the Treaty of Dominion was written to introduce new laws, ostensibly to guarantee peace, and to prevent the possibility of another district rebellion.
The Treaty''s most prominent provision is the establishment of the Hunger Trials. The event marks the anniversary of the districts'' defeat with a twisted annual celebration. District children between the ages of 12 and 18 are reaped via lottery to fight to the death in the Hunger Trials. Each year there are twenty-four tributes— one male and one female from each district— and they compete until only one remains as the victor.
The 10th Hunger Trials
For the first time, mentors are introduced into the Hunger Trials. They are chosen from the Academy''s top 24 students.
The reaping is held for the 10th Hunger Trials. The tributes begin their train journey by cattle car to the Capitol.
Tributes are unloaded at the train station and brought by truck to the Central Zoo.
The 10th Hunger Trials are hosted in the Capitol Coliseum. A tribute becomes District 7''s first victor.
The 25th Hunger Trials
The 25th Hunger Trials take place, operating under the unique rules of the first Quarter Quell: during the reaping, instead of being selected randomly, the tributes are elected by the citizens of their respective districts. The eventual victor of the First Quarter Quell is unknown and was deceased by the time of the Third Quarter Quell, half a century later. This was also the first year to have a designated arena for the specific purpose of hosting The Hunger Trials.
The 50th Hunger Trials
The card for the second Quarter Quell is read, declaring that twice the regular number of tributes will be selected in the reaping, resulting in a total of 48 tributes.
The 50th Hunger Trials take place.
The 50th Hunger Trials begin. 18 tributes die in the Cornucopia bloodbath.
A tribute is declared the victor of the 50th Hunger Trials.
Growing Unrest and the Second Rebellion (74 - 76 ADD)
The 74th Hunger Trials
The reaping is held for the 74th Hunger Trials. A tribute is reaped from District 7, but another tribute volunteers to take her place.
Arriving in the Capitol, the tributes are introduced to their stylists.
Training for the 74th Hunger Trials takes place.
The 74th Hunger Trials begin. Eleven tributes die in the bloodbath.
The Gamemakers start a forest fire to drive tributes together.','{"source": "Timeline.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 6, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Timeline.txt", "parent_document_id": "45df1921-83a8-43d8-9ea4-7c5aa0cf28ff"}','[-0.0039608744,0.08497799,-0.009737419,0.012315319,0.018347783,-0.023970064,-0.03594432,0.030734042,-0.015229281,-0.029643646,-0.05230079,-0.074789256,0.061999537,-0.048862975,-0.0009270276,-0.03907056,0.035011437,0.0020526217,-0.06758538,0.03451693,0.03897535,0.011835294,-0.010905764,-0.013759062,0.03906216,-0.0026641786,0.04777607,-0.034482207,-0.10038592,-0.0063309968,0.0022575282,-0.023778165,-0.013979696,0.06959474,0.004491973,0.007667932,0.003912562,-0.039853506,-0.0076643107,0.013117807,7.382954e-05,0.008696896,0.04589986,0.023306726,-0.012184731,0.037678577,-0.014752133,0.022545861,-0.017789118,-0.0257032,0.001597111,-0.054218605,-0.015676674,0.04124974,0.058364335,-0.0026278996,-0.011963807,0.0435561,-0.00025005292,0.0012460428,-0.008992942,-0.006717431,-0.0065738587,0.0277942,0.024598274,0.0070647504,-0.01654188,-0.040753637,-0.010572916,-0.0070233424,0.041052062,0.0058489917,0.03747577,0.0032586523,0.025689092,-0.04700542,-0.028666625,-0.023070678,0.0051234504,0.023825524,2.2321128e-05,-0.0141744185,-0.0016796226,-0.025543962,0.042042952,-0.02325952,-0.027795626,-0.017454164,0.015700469,-0.015262888,-0.0024349196,0.0110911,-0.0032331385,0.011885163,0.042573005,-0.013328284,-0.012879037,0.029386032,-0.027645629,0.021647265,-0.014233009,0.032779533,-0.00842807,-0.0032794941,-0.011988929,-0.002987628,-0.019773012,-0.02982762,-0.010161756,-0.02874395,0.010174207,-0.018439727,0.0013264035,0.022519885,-0.023729611,0.008795871,0.012207003,0.035860453,0.03781628,0.03890471,0.020369196,0.0037345935,-0.03328672,0.012071798,0.012740304,-0.0102870725,-0.014400179,-0.026845708,-0.00690422,0.0029983632,-0.030747749,-0.0064717694,