INSERT INTO public.vector_store (id,"content",metadata,embedding) VALUES
	 ('b4b0d6f1-1838-4407-84ae-8bb0445436d0'::uuid,'The remaining Careers recruit a tribute, who unearths, rearranges, and reactivates land mines to protect their supplies.
A young tribute is killed. Another tribute kills her attacker, and at the young tribute''s request, she sings the girl to sleep. Then she wreaths the body in flowers.
A rule change is announced: two tributes from the same district can win together if they''re the last two alive.
A feast is announced with items tributes desperately need.
The Gamemakers send a rainstorm.
The rain clears, so the tributes go hunting. While foraging, one tribute unknowingly collects poisonous Duskthorn berries, which another tribute steals and eats.
The final tributes are driven to the Cornucopia by wolf mutts.
Once the sun comes up at dawn, a tribute is mercy-killed. The remaining two tributes distance themselves, and then the rule change is revoked, attempting to pit them against each other. The two tributes attempt suicide by Duskthorn berries, but they are stopped by another announcement proclaiming them both the victors.
The tributes'' defiance inspires civil unrest throughout the nation.
Sometime after the conclusion of the 74th Hunger Trials, the Head Gamemaker is executed for permitting the dual victory.

74th Victory Tour
The victors leave District 7 by train.
They arrive in District 12 and give a speech. One victor promises that one month of their winnings from the Hunger Trials will go to the families of two deceased tributes, then the other victor thanks them for their assistance in survival in the Games. The district acknowledges their kindness with a three-finger salute. Sentinel Corps immediately execute an elderly citizen.
The victors visit multiple districts.
In the Capitol, one victor proposes to the other. The President makes a surprise appearance to congratulate them, but wordlessly communicates that they have failed to quell the unrest in the districts.
Meanwhile, a district uses the night''s special programming as an excuse to be out on the streets after dark, and they launch a full-scale uprising.
After this, the victors attend a party at the president''s mansion, and one victor meets the new Head Gamemaker. He shows her his The Final Ember watch, giving her a hint about the twist of the 75th Hunger Trials arena: that it will be like a clock, with a new threat in a particular section each hour.
The victors return to District 7.
Within forty-eight hours of its beginning, Sentinel Corps put down the district uprising. Afterwards, they institute a week-long lockdown, during which they air televised executions.
After a week, when the lockdown ends and regular work resumes, the Capitol bombs the district factory where the uprising had been planned.
Late 74 - early 75 ADD
A district''s Head Sentinel Corps is suddenly and quietly replaced.
A citizen is arrested for poaching and viciously whipped in the town square.
A victor is whipped across the face when attempting to intervene, but other victors are able to deescalate the situation.
The new Sentinel Corps backs down, and the victors and several coal miners are able to carry the citizen to the Champion''s Village for treatment.
The Sentinel Corps has machine gun nests placed on the rooftops of buildings, decorated their facades with patriotic banners, installed whipping posts, several stockades, and a gallows. He also has Sentinel Corps burn down a black market hub.
For two weeks, the mines stay closed, and half the district is starving. Children sign up for tesserae, but their grain and oil never arrives, and food shortages begin.
The mines reopen, wages are cut, and hours are increased. Parcel Day food deliveries arrive spoiled and defiled, and the price of food constantly increases.
The Sentinel Corps enforces long-ignored laws with his recent installations in the square.','{"source": "Timeline.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 2, "position": 2, "chunk_index": 2, "total_chunks": 6, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Timeline.txt", "parent_document_id": "45df1921-83a8-43d8-9ea4-7c5aa0cf28ff"}','[0.01708156,0.08274021,-0.0034619775,0.0017692358,0.0010145318,-0.024713125,-0.020082047,0.012947252,-0.015124513,0.023179773,-0.054262415,-0.078136325,0.039733272,-0.070867226,-0.014847695,-0.04584265,0.020488096,0.052599967,-0.04277665,0.04951835,0.032569434,0.02784321,0.009819062,-0.08598708,0.04079806,-0.010771273,0.053033713,-0.021084307,-0.13139217,0.005811014,0.002530878,-0.013663084,-0.010746907,0.06246347,0.023004794,-0.002062353,-0.017315991,0.009904762,0.008529788,-0.004151782,0.023281418,-0.004564446,0.02412727,0.015466719,-0.0051464895,0.038337197,0.014510045,-0.020267261,0.014282408,-0.029696053,0.009430418,-0.03142134,-0.021035064,0.036243867,0.04042971,0.024767196,0.007934193,0.01774041,-0.021712286,0.026537415,0.0022753857,0.024251489,-0.0005025082,0.028206626,0.022189958,0.0025249377,-0.006509964,-0.012675884,-0.017654153,0.004285961,0.031647164,0.01859763,0.021936188,-0.0014368995,0.040131163,-0.052879963,-0.050802883,-0.052607626,-0.0060125203,0.017418204,0.020613337,-0.025006838,-0.040053066,-0.036621388,0.03259568,-0.022332072,-0.021004643,-0.014445863,-0.0014522464,0.0038154284,-0.030480491,0.011296965,-0.039205156,0.03810603,0.016740888,-0.023152215,0.0040751197,0.0043539563,-0.03964251,0.02069166,-0.013229556,0.05731291,-0.020428006,-0.010217873,-0.012565307,-0.026486127,0.01920178,-0.022241523,0.025821796,-0.028309656,-0.032644626,-0.03758287,-0.0071914117,0.02130807,-0.00956458,-0.0067295413,-0.0056301053,0.02511368,0.02883462,0.047628332,0.044525597,0.0073850234,-0.009199417,0.0061818524,0.020021467,-8.470621e-05,0.012532683,-0.0072426074,0.008069313,0.020862225,-0.031289