	 ('111d2b49-3e05-49ca-b428-eeba0b9b39df'::uuid,'Selene Kade was the President of Sector 13 and a leader in the Second Rebellion. She orchestrated the Capital Loop bombing, clearing the way for her to become the interim President of Aurelia, before she was assassinated. Coin is the hidden secondary antagonist in the book The Final Ember.

Virtually nothing is known about Coin''s early life. As a woman in her fifties in The Final Ember, she was presumably born in Sector 13. At some point, she became the district''s president.

Coin arranged for the extraction of certain individuals from the Hunger Games arena. Priority was given to a symbolic figure for the rebellion, while another was captured and used as a propaganda asset by the Capitol.

Coin presented conditions for a symbolic deal, adding her own condition: that if the symbolic figure deviated from the rebels'' mission, the deal would be considered broken and Sector 13 law would decide their fates.

After a failed propaganda filming attempt, a meeting decided to send the symbolic figure into a less dangerous situation to evoke spontaneity: a visit to a heavily bombed district.

Coin presided over meetings reviewing propaganda broadcasts and planning further productions. She authorized security measures in response to a warning about an impending aerial strike, ordering a lockdown. She continued to give reports throughout the assault and later authorized the filming of a propaganda piece aboveground to show damage and assert survival.

During talks about a military operation, a suggestion was made to let Coin weigh in on the proposed plan. A decision was made and carried out. After this, all districts were unified against the Capitol.

Coin argued over the details of a wedding that would serve as an entertainment propaganda piece, vetoing certain elements.

Coin was confronted with a demand to be allowed to fight in a major battle. She assured the individual that their symbolic goal had been achieved and that they would be present for the surrender. She countered that others had attended regular training and set conditions for a case review.

Coin was reportedly unhappy with uninspiring propaganda footage. She personally assigned a brainwashed individual to join a squad, presumably an attempt to dispose of the symbolic figure amid the battle, making them a martyr and preventing them from becoming a threat to authority later. When the squad was presumed dead, Coin interrupted a broadcast to introduce herself as the head of the rebellion and to eulogize the symbolic figure.

Coin ordered that hovercraft falsely marked with the Capitol seal drop parachutes into a city circle. Children were primed to recognize these parachutes as offering aid, so they eagerly reached out to claim them. However, these were actually bombs. When peacekeepers and medics rushed in to help, they were killed by remaining parachutes. Believing the Capitol leader had massacred his own city''s children, any remaining supporters turned against him, and the war ended. A young medic was killed that day. Her presence was probably approved by President Coin herself.

After the Capitol leader''s arrest, Coin became the interim President of Aurelia. The former leader was tried and sentenced to death. To divert calls for outright genocide, Coin and her colleagues debated a proposal for another Hunger Games featuring the children of Capitol officials. She brought the proposal before the remaining victors and put it to a vote. The motion passed but was never carried out. The symbolic figure voted in favor to gain Coin''s trust. At the execution, Coin positioned herself on a balcony above everyone else. The symbolic figure turned their weapon against Coin, who collapsed over the side of the balcony and plummeted to the ground, dead.

Coin was described as being about 50 years old. She had gray hair that fell in an unbroken sheet to her shoulders. Her eyes were also gray.

On the surface, Coin appeared to have a calm and collected demeanor, but towards the end of the war, her ruthlessness in the pursuit of power became apparent.','{"source": "Alma Coin.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 0, "position": 0, "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 2, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Alma Coin.txt", "parent_document_id": "2f3a7a2a-399c-487f-bacb-4dcac9486dc9"}','[-0.0087158345,0.056114256,-0.01205046,0.009714975,-0.01657271,-0.052347116,-0.0037834293,0.01208846,-0.037450638,-0.03903909,-0.0729327,-0.08549489,0.05255103,-0.059443768,0.0076221502,0.011956026,0.02637172,0.041794512,-0.006453533,0.041132182,0.01390045,0.04336967,-0.017434837,-0.07592449,-0.024657687,0.020979885,0.021212144,0.004887441,-0.10801701,-0.00030210463,0.023903532,0.018115304,-0.030089699,0.030039076,0.011581562,0.0210345,0.0024419902,-0.0017378115,0.004174325,0.026711013,-0.03684631,-0.0109662395,-0.008788692,0.03061573,0.024330232,0.019395493,-0.022915708,-0.028781056,-0.022411508,-0.025541227,0.008312183,-0.044626057,0.01385005,-0.0013507406,0.049613338,0.035214934,0.010829938,0.037333626,0.017236615,-0.0028690274,-0.036530867,-0.0103757195,-0.004949101,0.023417547,0.0007288501,-0.010110496,0.024436649,-0.025812471,-0.017269507,0.008854461,0.024756713,-0.027804242,0.025482764,-0.0013603237,0.023087762,-0.01834942,-0.058956854,-0.009673348,0.026812127,0.0025453458,0.014918259,0.00067645346,-0.018309304,-0.03911729,0.05163961,-0.018784335,-0.032548785,-0.006746625,-0.009543764,-0.04045292,-0.034355078,0.049977303,-0.016121298,0.010458658,0.04142112,-0.05074366,-0.038708195,0.009140783,-0.027328122,0.024059314,0.012480189,0.012461438,-0.024284806,0.011978996,-0.0069574295,-0.020855058,-0.016050985,-0.007739386,0.02133057,-0.0355478,-0.018400656,0.021471271,-0.021306582,-0.0021609382,-0.035961863,-0.028550634,-0.018645898,0.04579943,0.019424403,0.06538231,0.0015505906,0.002473486,-0.029473707,0.047422517,-0.0012063477