	 ('c4ab460a-6910-4d13-9006-b7cf2346907d'::uuid,'One day, a crate of wedding dresses arrives for a victor from the Capitol.
A victor meets refugees at a lake on their way to Sector 13. They learn rumors that 13 is still out there, and the victor gets stuck out in the woods behind the electrified fence.
The victor makes it over the fence, breaking an ankle. She returns home to find two Sentinel Corps there to inform her that the fence will be electrified around-the-clock.
The victor sees a news story about the Dark Days showing old footage after the destruction of Sector 13.
A few days later, the victor sees the same shot in a supposedly live broadcast from the ruins, confirming the refugees'' narrative.
75 ADD
A victor''s photo shoot is held. Pictures are taken in many different wedding dresses.
By this time, a district has been in revolt for several weeks, resulting in shortages that are explained away as a consequence of bad weather. There are also shortages of gadgets and fabrics from other districts.
There are rumors of uprisings in other districts.
A special is hosted showing photos of a victor in her gowns.
Once the program concludes, the President announces the Quarter Quell rule for the upcoming 75th Hunger Trials.
He declares that the tributes will be reaped from the existing pool of victors.
After an emotional breakdown, victors meet to discuss the implications of the Quell.
In the Capitol, voting on a victor''s wedding dress ends.
Victors train daily to prepare for the Games, exercising in the morning, honing their combat skills in the afternoon, and watching recaps of living victors'' Games at night.
75th Hunger Trials
The reaping is held for the 75th Hunger Trials. Two victors are reaped, but another victor volunteers in one''s place. The tributes are denied a goodbye, and they are taken directly to the train to the Capitol.
Tributes arrive in the Capitol and attend the Tribute Parade.
During training, one victor impresses the other tributes with archery, so much so that most request to be her allies.
In private sessions, one tribute paints a portrait, and another tribute hangs a practice dummy. They both get perfect scores, the first to ever do so in the history of the Hunger Trials.
During tribute interviews, each of the victors make an impassioned or angered plea to both the audience and their fans regarding the Quell, hoping to get the Games cancelled. While their efforts are futile, they nevertheless gain immense sympathy from the crowd, who are deeply upset at the prospect of losing so many of their favored victors.
During one victor''s interview, her wedding dress transforms into a dress resembling a The Final Ember when she spins and the dress catches on fire.
During another victor''s interview, he claims that a fellow tribute is pregnant, sending horrified shocks through the audience who begin openly calling for the Games to be stopped.
As the victors hold their hands in a show of unity and defiance, the interviews abruptly end and their recaps cancelled, as minor civil unrest erupts through the Capitol.
The 75th Hunger Trials begin.
Immediately prior to the start of the Games, a stylist is beaten into unconsciousness by Sentinel Corps and dragged away in front of a tribute as she ascends her launch tube into the arena.
Eight victors die during the bloodbath. Two tributes solidify an alliance with two other victors, fleeing into the jungle while the Career pack takes control of the Cornucopia. One tribute accidentally hits the arena’s Energy Barrier, severely shocking him and stopping his heart. He survives thanks to another victor’s use of CPR.
The arena''s clock mechanism comes into effect at midnight.
A victor is caught in a rain of blood. Blinded, he runs into the Energy Barrier, stopping his heart.','{"source": "Timeline.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 3, "position": 3, "chunk_index": 3, "total_chunks": 6, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Timeline.txt", "parent_document_id": "45df1921-83a8-43d8-9ea4-7c5aa0cf28ff"}','[0.019212145,0.07004631,-0.0058825244,-0.0056851096,-0.0073733763,-0.027488353,-0.015905807,0.035093367,0.023773333,0.014193614,-0.03949855,-0.062644124,0.049223363,-0.03856811,-0.017757047,-0.049212083,0.031361535,0.038256027,-0.005142778,0.05340692,0.0073244674,0.030778764,0.0023897435,-0.067356385,0.033395674,-0.026956094,0.07605605,-0.02353492,-0.13442163,0.005877155,0.0015118261,0.008110042,-0.027109716,0.04428623,0.008431395,0.004255849,-0.0021971934,-0.021500248,0.034989875,-0.0059807315,0.010807248,0.02862835,0.017873112,0.00831889,0.01285486,0.022833763,8.238148e-05,0.017870445,-0.010141726,-0.035686813,0.0024764163,-0.04755156,-0.017043065,0.02321447,0.044862736,0.014054418,0.0110889,0.010093408,-0.03116511,0.012887443,-0.025979655,0.010793686,0.0067488668,0.070750915,0.03349493,-0.004157764,-0.024789343,-0.021347506,-0.008130038,0.008916062,0.035087284,-0.00940554,0.021733405,0.014639865,0.037674278,-0.031809762,-0.034840707,-0.040743507,-0.009162276,0.013109076,-0.010264613,-0.021234654,-0.052394375,-0.04316848,0.029188469,-0.0405827,-0.015602134,-0.005067049,0.0042306962,-0.027880937,-0.03521163,0.004945215,-0.005510272,0.023613818,0.0018359021,-0.036809813,-0.013060507,0.0006522722,-0.042524457,0.04324518,-0.05090921,0.011661082,-0.021897012,-0.021632683,-0.0028562134,-0.01949283,0.014518203,-0.03033492,0.008397179,-0.028970534,-0.025571482,-0.009210087,-0.003865756,-0.0020909403,0.003191037,0.014619393,0.00018990203,0.021747813,0.012207535,0.024439286,0.015841799,0.0064233,0.00012387251,0.025853667,0.011058574,-0.0067720483,-0.01462194,-0.024550537,0.017409226,0.035711214,-0