	 ('1104be4c-6510-47c5-be7c-513fdcc59a51'::uuid,'The Capitol was noted to contain the most powerful and wealthy families in all of Aurelia. Commonly, the Capitol citizens had inherited their wealth from the work of generations from their respective ancestors. As a result, old money and nepotism is especially prevalent within Capitol society. These affluent families were the most elite and powerful of all Aurelia citizens and were known to greatly influence political affairs impacting the rest of Aurelia.

The majority of Capitol citizens were noted to be "old money", that is, they inherited their wealth rather than earned it. The term described the most elite people''s maintenance of wealth and power over multiple generations, reflecting on the lifestyles of Capitol citizens. Capitol families with "old money" used their own assets and money to prevent the family from descending into the lower class. Before the Crimson Conflict "new money" was common, but after travel between the Districts was restricted, the last "new money" family emerged.
Although all citizens of the Capitol were of higher class, the most elite of the Capitol families would have avoxes attend to them alongside maids and servants. The wealthiest would also have many exclusive privileges such as entering the amphitheater in a private entrance away from the crowd.

Many Capitol citizens also lived in luxury penthouse apartments. The most powerful and wealthy citizens resided on the Corso, a palatial and grand residence with a wide avenue made of marble and granite. Some families owned a large mansion that took up an entire city block. The children of these families would attend the Academy, an elite secondary school. Those who showed promise at the Academy could continue their education at the University.
Families of the elite would also converse with one another exclusively. As such, some of the highest-status families would form exclusive groups and raise their children together.','{"source": "Capitol Families.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 0, "position": 0, "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 1, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Capitol Families.txt", "parent_document_id": "92440424-2ce1-487a-a654-33132f6790f8"}','[0.0001971513,0.09704396,-0.028365636,0.006132392,-0.010885678,-0.009419171,-0.008267057,-0.022542637,-0.037106186,0.020352291,-0.063013256,-0.050612483,0.044288374,-0.024393955,0.02353814,-0.006522285,0.012790416,0.10019463,0.023194004,0.045750026,0.036783393,0.06836881,-0.007406649,-0.041257028,-0.018988954,-0.026050065,0.022945236,0.037651144,-0.016059909,-0.00899395,-0.007426891,-0.008526312,0.0065866983,0.04645601,0.012982454,0.046988804,0.022786984,-0.03414663,0.028152045,-0.026794607,0.020562135,0.021360591,0.003279452,0.009920391,-0.008535383,0.022083014,-0.021075314,-0.023438964,0.02811626,0.014103533,0.0045504654,-0.05330938,0.019196384,0.034574732,0.026969304,-0.00047891433,-0.0025787717,0.03776586,-0.018261202,0.03071986,-0.00462007,0.04176498,-0.0099525945,0.020685283,0.037538722,-0.022301963,-0.024451993,-0.04192066,-0.017744979,-0.035633925,0.020963179,-0.006549669,-0.028133372,0.03454072,0.003416135,-0.030281348,-0.03496976,-0.004656365,0.032800168,0.052637953,-0.015968947,-0.0043210285,-0.03210709,-0.0023266408,0.016251875,-0.0094030835,0.029501315,-0.004081138,-0.022224622,-0.009961918,0.018616155,0.0055020778,0.017762244,0.045694195,-0.024669271,0.042293698,-0.02166818,-0.021637684,-0.01940955,0.031295042,0.014352175,-0.007209073,-0.033759817,0.0134763615,0.041403975,0.015466563,-0.001330548,-0.0019844973,0.044379767,0.00399449,-0.011053344,-0.024919549,0.018244013,0.0069096894,-0.03646128,-0.0057995594,-0.00082906254,0.02621973,-0.019718116,0.04172359,-0.02076244,0.018350217,-