	 ('b245afe1-f06f-4ad8-be13-af984ab003f3'::uuid,'President Gray was an autocrat who ruled as the tyrannical Chairman of Aurelia for more than two decades.

In his youth, he was known by a nickname.

Born into a wealthy family, by the time of his upbringing the family name had begun to fade into insignificance.

At a young age, he would lose both of his parents.

He later attended an academy, where he mentored the winning tribute of the 10th Hunger Trials.

He later moved on to advanced military studies at a university and served a brief stint in the Sentinel Corps, demonstrating such aptitude that he tested successfully for an elite program to become an officer, though ultimately, he did not pursue this path.

While attending the university and studying advanced military strategy, he also served as an apprentice Gamemaker, quickly instituting several new reforms to the Hunger Trials, including the creation of the Victors'' Village.

Frost would gradually eliminate his enemies one by one, until he finally ascended to the Presidency, the highest position offered in Aurelia and an office he presided, unchallenged, for over 25 years.

During this time, Aurelia became more authoritarian, with opponents of the regime regularly executed, and the Districts kept in line through the use of propaganda, intimidation, and brutality.

Major uprisings did not occur as a result, with many people being too afraid of the consequences they could face if they ever tried to rebel.

However, following the 74th Hunger Trials, the system that had kept the country in a state of fear and repression for decades finally began to come apart.

Events that took place in the arena gave life to a new and determined movement to end the regime.

As the Capitol began to crumble around him, Frost desperately tried to cling onto power, but in the end, he was unable to defeat the rebels.

Following the defeat of the Capitol, Frost would face the wrath of the same people he had terrorized for so long.

He is the main antagonist of a trilogy and is the main protagonist of a prequel novel.

As a youth, Frost had been raised on the belief that his family name meant prestige and power.

His experience, however, was tempered by the fact that he was an orphan and that the loss his family''s fortune meant that he had spent much of his early life in poverty, though he concealed this.

He was a studious student, one of the top-performing students at the academy.

He had a tendency to fixate on a single problem, convinced that if he could just fix it, then he could fix everything about his life.

His initial interactions with his tribute were based entirely on the idea that he needed to make her feel welcome. Over time, however, their interactions blossomed into genuine affection. He eventually did come to love her, but in the end chose to eschew love in exchange for power and ambition. Filled with ideas of control and power, he made it his ambition to rule over all others.

By the time he was president, any of the few positive qualities he had from his youth were largely unrecognizable. He had become exactly what he had set out to achieve. He was a ruthlessly cruel, sadistic, wrathful, violent, greedy, arrogant, power-hungry, wicked and purely and utterly evil man, one obsessed with keeping the perfection of the established order and maintaining absolutely no respect or care for human life. He was an extremely tyrannical, megalomaniacal, and egomaniacal ruler who ruled over Aurelia with an iron fist. He constantly threatened and killed people who stood in his way to holding absolute power. He was not hesitant to use people for his personal advantage.

His obsession with perfection arises out of his paranoia due to his fear of losing power.','{"source": "Coriolanus Snow.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 0, "position": 0, "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 4, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Coriolanus Snow.txt", "parent_document_id": "6dde718f-7f32-4ddf-aef0-d37954f9f4d6"}','[0.014323133,0.09016195,-0.011312439,-0.0088486,-0.009505441,-0.06872744,-0.024207423,-0.0068308115,-0.014927953,-0.036776286,-0.04510076,-0.089922994,0.023411948,-0.015864724,-0.008489084,-0.012641353,0.03612328,0.02075509,0.012105629,0.03024114,-0.005474761,0.019661667,0.03422231,-0.05130947,0.012760006,0.013555637,0.01993209,0.05564018,-0.08055871,0.006123345,0.01884522,-0.0030098113,0.020317975,0.028804125,0.017384894,0.061090905,0.0039891875,-0.018310755,0.0028896937,-0.027750187,0.025087463,0.0008440174,-0.008416835,0.049003195,-0.03653841,-0.037759606,1.9580284e-05,0.0031870557,-0.00238724,0.0057617994,-0.016976217,-0.045394365,0.040232603,0.011024119,0.025094008,-0.019411732,-0.016678076,0.04034394,0.008332121,0.03922158,-0.029921737,0.03970282,-0.0064383177,-0.015493814,0.0005193915,-0.0064694947,0.013192517,-0.019949779,-0.032438405,-0.0131187,0.023634609,-0.0068017105,-0.0072214045,0.0049827895,-0.008101879,-0.012600061,-0.028768562,-0.019968666,0.015452691,0.017785529,0.027309872,-0.021983078,-0.013777146,-0.035900187,0.04023218,-0.031198317,-0.01533259,-0.002740109,-0.0037378143,-0.034143165,-0.011010648,0.022540636,0.026265403,0.029268842,0.027932351,-0.02681595,0.024034834,0.0026759822,-0.022321032,0.012429213,0.018902056,-0.008656019,-0.023428662,0.017192349,0.011675954,-0.0077456143,0.0014926752,0.014159069,0.021307115,-0.01416298,-0.041655134,-0.009732392,-0.0106457425,-0.027441503,-0.009035222,-0.0075947675,-0.039857034,0.0043159127,-0.015360832,0.044523954,-0.0038146423,0.010949477,-0.026122859,0.02656093,-0.013308091,-0.027380498,-0.026250662,0.019661179,-0.04016553