	 ('010f3812-303a-471b-9d96-2224df278e59'::uuid,'As a result, he murdered allies and enemies alike, usually by poisoning them, and in his effort to throw off suspicion he drunk his own murderous poison from the same cup and was left with a mouthful of bloody sores which are the only outward sign of his insanity. He uses the thick perfume of genetically enhanced roses in his lapel to cover the scent of his bloody mouth.

Noticeably, Frost was an extremely calm and reserved man, never visibly losing his temper at any point. He remained completely in control, both figuratively and literally, throughout a conversation and maintained his serenity even if his life were in danger or if he were facing a known enemy. He had absolutely no lapses when it came to discussing the execution or omission of other people. He also suggested that his successor was more dangerous than he was.

His name and his white roses symbolize his mental need to appear flawless, despite his obvious flaws. Despite all this, he claims that he is not wasteful. He has a very clear understanding of the districts'' emotions towards the Capitol, and how fear doesn''t make them back down if they have hope- which he allows, in a very limited form, as a motivator. He''ll only kill people for well-defined reasons. He is also willing to take the life of children for his own safety. He was obviously highly intelligent and cunning as evidenced by his manipulation and his ability to maintain control for at least 25 years. At the very least, he was quite capable of admitting that he had been overwhelmed, outwitted and defeated because of some of his own mistakes and shortcomings.

To the very end, Frost showed no remorse for his tyranny and murderous desire for power, often acting self-righteous and blaming the disruption of the status quo, reasoning that for all his authoritarian propaganda he believed the games insured order and control.

The President was a small, thin man, with paper-white hair and thick lips that seem pulled across his face. His lips were thought to be changed, to make them look fuller and more appealing. He always smelled strongly of genetically enhanced roses. He always wore a white rose in his lapel to cover the scent of blood. His eyes were similar to a snake''s. Overall, his appearance was quite snake-like. His trademark sign was a single white rose.

As an 18-year-old, President Gray was very good-looking. He had pale blue eyes, blond curls, a trim and athletic physique, and excellent posture. He was not as tall as he could have been since malnourishment during the war stinted his growth.

Frost resided in a huge mansion where he sometimes hosted parties. It is described as being large enough "to get lost in." The mansion contains many rooms. There is also an internal greenhouse for Frost''s roses in a section of the mansion.

He is known to have a granddaughter. This also means he must have had at least one child.

After a certain Hunger Trials, he was angry that two tributes managed to both be crowned victors but acted calm while visiting. He pushed one enough to agree not to lie to each other. While the tributes were in a later Hunger Trials arena, one managed to destroy it, further angering him, and he subsequently ordered a district to be firebombed, destroying it and wiping out the majority of the population. He continued to engage in a twisted game of psychological manipulation, though methods such as leaving roses, torturing a victor and forcing him to make various interviews, and hijacking that victor to turn his love into a weapon for the purpose of killing the other victor.

After his trial, he was the only one to offer condolences for a death and revealed his successor''s role in a bombing. However, this was most likely out of a desire to get revenge, rather than being rooted in remorse and a desire to atone for his wrongdoing. The victor subsequently realized that Frost was right.','{"source": "Coriolanus Snow.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 4, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Coriolanus Snow.txt", "parent_document_id": "6dde718f-7f32-4ddf-aef0-d37954f9f4d6"}','[-0.008134952,0.047428712,0.0052328887,0.019656237,-0.012049835,-0.0814722,-0.0150962835,-0.009191417,-0.011229789,-0.030865746,-0.04100274,-0.051521927,0.038920395,-0.036340754,-0.03557418,-0.012494511,0.05081968,0.01713392,0.038177013,0.053052288,0.002230129,0.027446125,-0.017574731,-0.063706,-0.008684767,0.059874747,-0.0031881528,0.034156855,-0.10556366,0.027946334,0.0582702,-0.00097047514,0.009748421,0.00847238,-0.006455138,0.050485663,-0.01126757,-0.0028967054,0.023896342,-0.026281398,0.0066205193,0.00079251616,0.037960153,0.030672647,-0.008793484,-0.025311,-0.003547174,-0.003009573,0.013504435,-0.021337198,-0.02306402,-0.044957507,0.03198588,0.008126817,0.019023227,-0.016735187,-0.0023877553,0.041517045,-0.02733861,0.012043942,-0.02586711,0.028430223,0.0031926304,0.022097368,-0.0009252375,-0.026596483,0.019990176,-0.0069818553,-0.020396514,0.013227187,0.013296874,-0.0069607594,0.028429793,0.004456937,-0.01631147,-0.02173517,-0.060036305,-0.04767858,0.016426168,0.030549217,0.0346986,-0.00014093981,-0.028165525,-0.030372085,0.04191234,-0.034891997,-0.011586177,-0.012621297,-0.012736193,0.022740755,-0.039845996,0.029424924,0.016632823,0.032600712,0.009757077,-0.0027375752,0.0042298627,0.011297423,-0.020574158,0.012294167,0.0077421446,0.026245166,-0.002633945,-0.014677952,0.0032569598,0.00014072945,0.011072795,-0.012834538,0.0218117,-0.035426322,-0.03904661,-0.0093