	 ('2fa21390-901c-44e4-8f57-a1a0c6cfb256'::uuid,'The friend, remorseful over a death, believes they should die rather than endanger the rest of the squad again, but admits that memories are becoming clearer. The President, discovering the protagonist is still alive, unleashes a pack of monstrous reptilian Hybrid Mutants to hunt the protagonist down. In the ensuing battle, several squad members are killed. As the squad attempts to flee the sewers, a mutt grabs a friend as they cover the retreat, forcing the protagonist to use the holographic map''s self-destruct to end the suffering and destroy the remaining mutts. They are attacked after reaching the underground railways, during which another trap kills another member. The few survivors eventually reach the surface and are led to a safehouse, where a former stylist hides them. While they all mourn the loss of their squad, the protagonist confesses to lying about the orders to kill the President, and as a result of the lie, the rest of the squad are dead. The squad reveal that they knew this all along, but played along because they trusted the protagonist. The friend comforts the protagonist, saying that if the President is killed, it will avenge the deaths of everyone who has died because of him. That night, two friends discuss their relationship, with one stating they think the other has won over the protagonist, but the other thinks the opposite. One eventually remarks that deciding which one the protagonist can''t live without is the protagonist''s problem.

The President announces that the rebels have penetrated deep and asks refugees to come to the mansion, offering them food and shelter. With the traps deactivated to allow passage, the protagonist and a friend disguise themselves and mingle with the refugees to gain access. Their covers are nearly blown when the rebels arrive and attack the forces, killing many civilians. In the ensuing chaos, the friend is captured; the protagonist marches towards the mansion and finds forces taking children to provide a human shield. As the rebels near the mansion, a SkyGlider flies by and drops Gold parachute into the crowd of children surrounding the mansion, which explode. Upon the explosion, a team of rebel medics attempt to help the injured, among whom is the protagonist''s sister. Shocked to see the sister on the battlefield, the protagonist heads towards her, but just as the sister is seen a second round of bombs go off, killing the sister and badly injuring the protagonist.

Upon recovering, the protagonist learns that the Capitol has been conquered by the rebels, and that the President has been captured. The protagonist confronts the imprisoned President, who claims that the rebel leader masterminded the child-bombings in order to turn remaining supporters against him; the rebel leader has thus played both the President and the protagonist because they were both too focused on destroying each other to see the endgame. When accused of lying, the President calmly reminds of a promise to always be truthful to each other. Suspicious, the protagonist realizes that the bombs resembled a trap that had been worked on earlier. When confronting the friend, the friend remorsefully confesses that it may have been their design and apologizes for failing to protect the family; unable to fully forgive, the protagonist says goodbye.

Later, the protagonist attends a meeting with the rebel leader and the other surviving victors. The leader proposes having one final edition of the Hunger Games with the children of the Capitol as retribution for the previous games, as an alternative to exterminating most of the Capitol''s population as war criminals. Some vote no, while others vote yes. Realizing that the President was right about the leader''s ambitions and ruthlessness, the protagonist votes in favor of the motion, which gains the leader''s trust; another follows the lead. The protagonist is awarded the opportunity to execute the President.

At the execution, which is being held before the whole nation, the protagonist faces the President once again. As the bow is readied, the two make eye contact, and the President gives one last smile.','{"source": "The Hunger Games_ Mockingjay - Part 2.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 3, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/The Hunger Games_ Mockingjay - Part 2.txt", "parent_document_id": "31b34683-3695-44de-93ea-e0959c64d14a"}','[0.0113590835,0.0817411,-0.008765187,0.013564715,0.007626991,-0.046156354,0.016722608,0.01063553,-0.024187703,0.01666185,-0.087299585,-0.08065014,0.058937583,-0.048345648,-0.011141641,0.0021812504,0.03606278,0.050415084,-0.011594731,0.06416899,-0.007003556,-0.0031253442,-0.026809366,-0.056881726,-0.011964283,0.001404159,0.0365564,-0.005953098,-0.10856494,0.015980419,0.034206502,0.037366565,0.0132307615,0.027529912,0.005464174,0.018089695,-0.0036454187,0.00300771,0.0095241405,-0.006006068,0.018627785,0.010675446,0.026086828,-0.016213743,-0.00018777142,0.011470822,-0.03369502,-0.025807526,-0.003433515,-0.024170622,0.0013055273,-0.03142742,0.021332841,-0.012832083,0.033462364,-0.0077452087,-0.019439528,0.042959813,-0.028018948,0.025588555,0.0009175144,-0.018912472,0.0020091445,0.029218996,0.004917992,-0.017859206,0.01192439,-0.008760643,-0.03163835,0.009979038,0.048414376,-0.0074871285,0.0011738441,0.014289623,-0.0005886202,-0.024163231,-0.057536036,-0.01875816,0.013433787,0.010822485,0.02644451,-0.012605053,-0.019008895,-0.036267545,0.039843466,-0.04183371,-0.018766893,-0.00954241,0.0170285,-0.015966093,-0.03915097,0.032362122,0.014479812,0.027448183,-0.0043961788,-0.023334103,-0.004343394,0.02823003,-0.024096228,0.021564832,0.016451012,0.00977939,-0.014638203,0.025809264,0.009335312,-0.018636461,-0.007623467,0.0055750213,0.029412346,-0.022219254,-0.034281097,-0.003222163,0.01075213,-0.02669275,-0.028276112,-0.054334678,0.005898837,0.010