	 ('dad60335-8f6a-4e47-bb13-dd80e3223cf7'::uuid,'The mentor is then confronted with evidence against him, including the token and the handkerchief he dropped into the snake tank. Thus, he becomes a Peacekeeper.

The new Peacekeeper asks to be assigned to District 7, an uncommon request that is granted. He had been told that while they had overlooked some rule-breaking for all mentors, his specific actions couldn''t be overlooked. He was given the alternative of avoiding public disgrace by joining the Peacekeepers. As he shipped out, there was no coverage of the games on television.

He arrives in District 7 and meets fellow recruits. He settles into a routine and learns from a letter that his family apartment is going on the market. He despairs and considers suicide when he hears a familiar voice: the other mentor. He is thrilled to see him. The other mentor explains his situation was similar; he was on the verge of expulsion, but his father made a deal for him to graduate and enroll in the Peacekeepers, on the condition that the new Peacekeeper be allowed to graduate also. He presents a diploma, saying he graduated with honors and can take the officer test.

It''s announced there''s going to be a band performance where his tribute will be singing. He realizes it is his chance to finally see her. He and the other mentor receive a package of food they can trade for entry. Before the day, however, they are ordered to attend a hanging. As the execution proceeds, a woman shouts. The man shouts a warning before he is hung, and the call is rebounded and echoed by birds in the trees, identified as jabberjays. The sound is transformed into something melodic by mockingjays. The Peacekeeper dislikes them on sight and suggests creating a hunting party to rid the woods of them.

The time comes for the performance. His tribute appears and sings. He is pleased to see her but worried she might not be his girl. She finally sees him and sings a song he knows is for him. During their reunion, there is a disturbance from a drunk man who is clearly her spurned former lover. Others order him away. Peacekeepers try to send him away and it looks like a fight when the lights go on. Everything becomes chaos and both Peacekeepers end up taking the mayor''s daughter home. There, he sees the former lover.

The next morning, no soldier may leave the base alone. The other mentor offers to accompany him to his tribute''s home. He secures a bag of ice. They travel and a girl guides him to his tribute. He finds her in a meadow, singing a song. She tells him he found her. She thanks him for the ice and, at his request, tells him more about the arena. In return, he tells her the truth about why she was able to charm the snakes. She says they both saved each other and that they''re together. She also tells him the dean gave her money on the quiet, apologizing, leading him to wonder why.

She takes him inside, hoping to introduce him to others, but the former lover is back. Furthermore, the other mentor is talking with him. He tells them not to worry. She warns the former lover to go away. He implies she plays with men''s hearts. She tells him this isn''t true. She didn''t come back for more of the same and he tells her to make a new life with him. They agree to meet the next week. On the way back, he learns the other mentor was talking about the captured woman from the hanging. She''s been locked up and he''s agreed to try to get information. He is shocked, telling him he''s not thinking properly. The other mentor asks if he thinks he''s committed treason and he says not quite yet. The other mentor reveals that a high official thought he did, and his father bought her off. He agrees to be more careful.','{"source": "The Ballad of Songbirds and Snakes_Summary.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 2, "position": 2, "chunk_index": 2, "total_chunks": 6, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/The Ballad of Songbirds and Snakes_Summary.txt", "parent_document_id": "24c698c4-dc4b-41aa-9335-49cc2f4a0b42"}','[0.02545822,0.025594315,0.03585638,0.0069778147,-0.0023860591,-0.036132485,0.00031602412,-0.018436119,-0.015653798,0.0052747806,-0.067805134,-0.06896833,0.06380743,-0.02543718,-0.06362225,-0.015504051,0.032946486,0.0049653784,-0.036271732,0.07375674,-0.008884461,0.034910683,0.029916497,-0.07586065,2.9415633e-05,0.015580613,0.037635285,0.0053985417,-0.10919248,0.020467147,0.008866458,0.028579747,-0.007748538,0.050026853,-0.008155386,0.0458737,0.045056663,0.021838468,0.025475493,-0.017390858,-0.009012209,0.016067011,-0.016144127,0.012123645,-0.015051531,-0.011659529,0.026657134,-0.005238153,-0.037041526,-0.04322393,0.016942488,-0.044922538,-0.010134714,0.014875217,0.0081852125,0.016005415,-0.020910317,0.034990884,-0.035747096,0.029551405,-0.001083856,0.023512311,-0.033316646,-0.0005695942,-0.0035267633,-0.016