	 ('fbe0e61e-7bc9-4edf-aaa9-1dadd32d5b62'::uuid,'He then shoots in her direction and she collapses. He shouts at his tribute to get back onstage for an alibi, but the former lover charges, saying if he swings, she does, so the other man shoots him through the chest. The other man tells his tribute to go before someone comes and he promises to take care of it. They all promise to keep it quiet, though the other man suggests he might want to think about coming with them. He and the other mentor return to base. As time passes, he begins to relax, sure nothing can tie him to the crime, and that he can get the other mentor to give up the escape plan. However, the other man is brought in on a stretcher. The next morning, the other mentor is arrested. He is quickly executed for treason, the jabberjays calling out his last word.

He becomes convinced it will only be a matter of time until he is arrested too, worried over the rifle. He decides to face death and is relieved when summoned. He is thanked for his sacrifice, given he was close friends with the executed mentor. He is asked about guns, if perhaps they were bought on the black market. In the end, he is told he did a real service and to enjoy a party. He celebrates by blasting mockingjays and that evening, listens to his tribute singing a new song about him. Afterwards, she tells him the mayor believes she killed both the mayor''s daughter and the former lover and that she''s going to run away north. She says she''s glad to say good-bye, but he replies he''s going with her. She says he''d be risking his life, but he replies it''s only a matter of time until they find the guns and connect him to the murder. They agree to meet at dawn.

That morning, as he prepares to meet her, he is intercepted and told he''s wanted in the commander''s office. He fears he has been caught, but is told he leaves for officers'' school the next day. He''s the youngest ever to pass the test and is recommended for an elite program. He is bitter at the irony, that his second chance is stripped away by the murder weapon. He steels himself and goes to find her. He asks about her group, but she says she''s wearing out her welcome and was told not to sing a certain dark song again. They set off, she saying she''ll miss her music and birds and he saying he won''t miss people. He lets slip a comment about having killed three people, referencing the executed mentor. When she confronts him, he tells her he killed the old him so he could come with her.

They take shelter from the rain in an old shack and there, he is stunned to discover a bag containing weapons, including the one with his DNA. He asks if they should take them and she says she doesn''t trust them, telling him she''s going to dig up some plants. With her gone, he hatches a new plan. He can destroy the gun, and there will be nothing tying him to the crime. He loves her, but he can''t stand the thought of life in the wilderness. He wonders how she will react. He goes out to find her and realizes she''s hiding. He can think of only one reason: that she''s figured out the truth of his wanting to run away, and that he had betrayed the other mentor. He shouts for her, saying he just wants to talk, but gets no reply. He searches and finds her scarf, then is bit by a snake the scarf was covering. He is shocked that she has apparently tried to kill him and does not know what to do. He yells out to her again, telling her it''s not too late, and in response, she sings from the dark song.','{"source": "The Ballad of Songbirds and Snakes_Summary.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 4, "position": 4, "chunk_index": 4, "total_chunks": 6, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/The Ballad of Songbirds and Snakes_Summary.txt", "parent_document_id": "24c698c4-dc4b-41aa-9335-49cc2f4a0b42"}','[0.00491649,0.035378173,0.018746046,-0.00784815,-0.0057106093,-0.014064721,0.028330822,-0.019564105,-0.042868752,-0.009244722,-0.076505125,-0.05406142,0.055187043,-0.030379327,-0.023859167,0.00842352,0.066815324,0.02305025,0.011129783,0.056416005,-0.013460218,0.0063256277,0.0019531564,-0.07425882,-0.02080247,0.013151377,0.03138316,-0.010672221,-0.10699266,0.035645716,0.008986054,0.06332649,-0.011314978,0.040152274,0.017808408,0.025577476,0.043777846,0.009246682,0.0054070493,-0.021972803,0.0077457307,0.028816741,0.009548826,-0.0066525606,0.009663235,-0.00031033452,0.015276054,-0.003651558,-0.006158752,-0.06252631,0.026676185,-0.048004