	 ('73b442c2-c428-471c-a7bf-adaf7decd5bd'::uuid,'The Command Center is where the main events of the Hunger Games are controlled and headed, such as the chariot rides, interviews, and training scores. The Hunger Games are operated by the Game Master from this room.

In the film, the Command Center shows a large holographic view of the arena on the circular center console. There are two semicircles of seated Game Master and tables on both sides, each with holographic screens in front of them. The room has blue, futuristic lighting.
On their screens, Game Master can monitor each tribute''s status, location, and decide who to focus the cameras on. They can alter the temperature, change the apparent time of day, trigger traps, and create and unleash Hybrid Mutants.

For a subsequent Games, a different control room is shown. The room is almost identical in layout, with the addition of an office for the Head Game Master on the upper level.
Viewers of the Hunger Games were shown the control room, but it was not revealed to them that there was, in fact, a secret Game Master level within the arena itself, in order to maintain the illusion of the Games being controlled from afar. This was an entirely subterranean floor, which managed manual tasks such as unleashing Hybrid Mutants or stocking a feast, though this was all secondary to the real job of managing the onsite computer system that was central to running the Games.','{"source": "Control Room.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 0, "position": 0, "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 1, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Control Room.txt", "parent_document_id": "760d331b-aacc-411e-b0c7-6b7046fa535a"}','[0.042622052,0.03995337,-0.037215695,0.019383144,0.00042772427,-0.07045025,-0.00318568,-0.026246374,0.02755383,0.035175405,-0.036561925,-0.07080182,0.058832977,-0.013396855,0.009174531,-0.020890566,-0.015886707,0.07597411,-0.0625496,0.052803285,0.019577065,0.017212823,-0.026149282,-0.033365536,0.0019452354,0.046144992,0.032401808,-0.033856027,-0.07200612,-0.029765064,-0.027648294,0.030992739,0.018127369,0.040918525,-0.03193372,0.020833937,-0.015243286,0.037163243,-0.0040638307,-0.02309793,0.015556539,0.017501839,-0.0018335098,0.017194418,0.006746629,0.03559102,0.006677326,-0.0020588052,-0.014457715,-0.034685526,0.030780133,-0.045335013,-0.048066758,0.007125721,0.017314993,0.0028999168,-0.022231076,-0.0040025925,-0.026533358,-0.0018717716,0.008270795,0.03139332,-0.014354045,0.059282303,0.0026015872,0.005892606,-0.002344409,0.0007615081,-0.009851361,0.015513517,0.053076595,0.0006949536,-0.0015068403,0.013474104,-0.012054545,0.02691857,-0.05182214,-0.029456176,0.0031125417,0.03390105,0.03333025,-0.06680751,-0.02310348,-0.04251431,-0.014767434,-0.0043628863,0.0015586767,-0.009102937,0.023740364,-0.025301127,-0.013760203,0.040130164,-0.009863097,0.031090068,0.014121957,-0.01373554,0.01965311,0.038519662,-0.