	 ('0c3dea75-a403-49e5-9f95-78cacd65f7d5'::uuid,'The Fire Games: The Ballad of Songbirds & Snakes is an American dystopian film. It is the fifth installment in the film franchise. It was released theatrically on November 17, 2023.

As one of the top students at the Academy, a school for the Capitol''s elite, Corin Snow is selected to mentor Lena Jansen, District 7''s female tribute, in the 10th Hunger Games. As he works with Lucy Gray, the two grow close together, leading Snow on an unexpected rise to power as he fights to make sure Lucy Gray wins the Hunger Games at any cost.

Three years before the 1st Hunger Games, a young Corin Snow is led by his cousin through the ruined streets of the Capitol. They locate food, but they''re confronted by a rabid dog. However, while hiding, they see an otherwise respectable man kneeling and chopping off the leg of a corpse. When Corin Snow asks why he would do that, the reply is that he''s starving. They make their way home safely, but inside their apartment, the Grandma''am is flanked by two Peacekeepers, and she explains that Coriolanus''s father has been killed by a rebel trap in the woods outside District 7.

13 years later, Corin Snow is now in his senior year at the Academy. It is the day of the reaping ceremony, and tensions run high for the Victory Prize—a prize awarded to the highest achieving student upon graduation, giving them access to the highest reaches of the government and paying their university tuition. Ever since the war began, the Snow family has fallen into tough times, and the Victory Prize is a necessity for Corin Snow to attend the University.

In the morning, Coriolanus cannot find his father''s dress shirt, which he plans to wear to the reaping. However, his cousin returns it to him after fashioning the shirt. Coriolanus thanks her and leaves for the Academy.

As the anthem plays and the students get into their seats, the Head Gamemaker begins to speak, having high hopes of the new generation and introducing the Dean, the creator of the Hunger Games.

The Dean continues with the speech, announcing that the Capitol citizens have grown bored of the Games. Now the Victory Prize winner will not be based on grades, but instead awarded to the best mentor in the Hunger Games, who can persuade their district tribute to perform for the cameras. A classmate complains about the possibility of being assigned a weak tribute, but the Dean corrects her by saying that their role is to turn these tribute into spectacles, not survivors.

Once the reaping starts, at last, Coriolanus is assigned the District 7 girl, Lena Jansen. During the reaping, Lucy Gray drops a snake down the dress of the of District 7 Mayor''s daughter. She then sings a song, getting attention from everyone and charming Coriolanus.

In a private conversation with the Dean, Coriolanus learns that the Dean is well aware of his family''s poverty, despite his best efforts to hide it. Furthermore, the Dean seems to possess an inexplicable grudge against him. At night, the cousin suggests that Coriolanus make Lucy Gray trust him, so she can sing to attract an audience.

Coriolanus decides to visit Lucy Gray at the train station, where the tributes will be arriving in cattle cars. Lucy Gray seems unimpressed with Coriolanus, who gave her a white rose. He then follows her to a cargo car with the other tributes, intent on accompanying her to her quarters. In the cargo car, he nearly gets strangled by a tribute. The car dumps them into the old monkey enclosure in the Capitol Zoo, where the tributes will be put on display before the Games.

They are greeted by a weatherman and amateur magician who will be hosting the 10th Hunger Games.','{"source": "The Hunger Games_ The Ballad of Songbirds & Snakes.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 0, "position": 0, "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 4, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/The Hunger Games_ The Ballad of Songbirds & Snakes.txt", "parent_document_id": "90c853d9-d25f-40ac-940f-76e07c756734"}','[0.064209476,0.048297923,0.016643912,-0.052345924,-0.007828079,-0.038261835,0.01781859,0.015815742,0.01499421,0.025908237,-0.054260906,-0.12066164,0.034283407,-0.014430869,-0.04617873,-0.039818607,0.007801703,0.082204826,0.01728912,0.020027474,0.0018383127,0.04197337,-0.028150637,-0.07671552,0.033332307,0.0025483111,0.07344615,0.011099286,-0.101098284,0.011068093,0.04066746,0.02951895,0.0141565455,0.052905675,-0.013866105,0.06666002,0.012701687,0.003390199,0.022294004,-0.015991876,0.01812594,0.0017067089,-0.009335591,0.036275424,0.027455127,-0.038209174,0.03827488,-0.0053017153,0.020222893,-0.018719498,0.02441725,-0.03567526,-0.011304145,0.012660721,0.0069980104,-0.0038848212,-0.0090679545,0.023700994,-0.009090711,0.011677036,-0.01912064,0.024766864,0.009755375,0.054117583,-0.0098171225,-0.028182574,0.020652233,-0.022902373,-0.017173437,0.013414391,0.031410288,0.0075738383,8.087112e-05,-0.014186661,0.016639208,-0.0067652534,-0.053647354,-0.052880354,-0.030412514,-0.016003644,0.043356504,-0.037808515,-0.038711235,-0.023916066,0.008162302,-0.04176343,0.008717235,0.0043257987,0.02327008,0.000459295,0.0074752467,0.0332237,-0.04302842,0.033849318,-0.005713133,-0.039854042,0.0023671119,0.009722322,-0.022209393,0.03905716,0.0070400885,0.013839749,-0.040053096,-0.0142129995,0.028241405,0.007520397,-0.026561324,-0.022628011,0.018078277,-0.029369501,-0.016034463,-0.028609505,0.0057125036,0.038478795,-0.007054507,-0.026493559,0.014967214,0.019872323,0.035051852,0.0342732,0.03437361,0.011114788,-0.06496715,0.02489387,-0.00