	 ('69dc5eb6-87e6-4d91-bc19-058d55b51ce8'::uuid,'Coriolanus puts the white rose into Lucy Gray''s hair and presents her to the Capitol audience at the Zoo. Lucy Gray''s dress garners lots of attention from the children. She reveals that she was not originally from District 7, but part of a traveling music group known as the Covey and got trapped in District 7 following the war. Lucy Gray also asks Coriolanus to bring food for her and the other District 7 tribute, Jessup, as neither have eaten since the reaping.

Coriolanus arrives at a mentor meeting, where the Dean expresses great disappointment in his actions and threatens to disqualify him as mentor. A classmate adds on that Coriolanus is making it seem they''re the same as these "animals". Another mentor then defends Snow, stating that the tributes are human beings and that''s why no one watches the Games. However, the Head Gamemaker interrupts. She was very pleased with Coriolanus visiting Lucy Gray and suggests he should be a Gamemaker, like her. The Head Gamemaker then asks him what the Hunger Games are for, and Coriolanus answers that they''re to punish the districts—an answer that the Head Gamemaker is unsatisfied with. The other mentor questions the morality of the Games, making the Dean agree with him. Coriolanus snaps back, suggesting that they can allow the citizens to place bets on the tributes and interview them, so they actually care about what happen to these tributes. His classmate suggests that she and Coriolanus work on this project together, hoping to take the credit.

In the cafeteria, the other mentor reveals to Coriolanus that his tribute was his classmate back in his home district and that his father bought him just to show him that he can never go back to the districts. They head to the zoo in the hopes of interacting with and feeding their tributes. The other mentor''s tribute ignores him, and Coriolanus gives a sandwich to Lucy Gray. She shares it with Jessup, who had been bitten by a bat. Coriolanus tells her that he might be able to send her food in the arena and tries to convince her to sing again. Lucy Gray notices Coriolanus staring hungrily at the sandwich, so she also shares some with him. Their conversation stops when another mentor''s tribute slits her mentor''s throat with a broken bottle, killing her. The tribute is shot dead by Peacekeepers, being the first tribute to die. In the apartment, the Grandma''am warns Coriolanus of Lucy Gray.

The next day, the tributes and mentors have their first official meeting, during which most mentors fail to get their tributes to comply. The classmate and Coriolanus are invited to meet the Head Gamemaker. The classmate panics, as Coriolanus wrote their assignment without her help. Having realized the truth, the Head Gamemaker has her retrieve the project page from a tank of snake mutts. Not recognizing her scent, the snakes bite the classmate, who is taken away unconscious.

The mentors and tribute tour the arena the next day. One tribute gets recruited into an alliance, leaving his betrayed district partner behind. Soon, bombs start going off, killing several tributes and severely injuring a mentor. Two tributes escape with the other mentor''s tribute when an exit is bombed opened—although they are immediately shot. Instead of running, Lucy Gray chooses to save Coriolanus from burning debris. Coriolanus wakes up in the hospital and watches Lucy Gray sing a song about her past lover back home for the interviews, gaining many sponsor donations. Coriolanus returns the favour of Lucy Gray saving his life  by secretly going into the bombed, rubble filled arena, discovering tunnels she can hide in and also giving her his mother''s compact filled with rat poison. Lucy Gray tells him about her former boyfriend, who caught the attention of the Mayor''s daughter.','{"source": "The Hunger Games_ The Ballad of Songbirds & Snakes.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 4, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/The Hunger Games_ The Ballad of Songbirds & Snakes.txt", "parent_document_id": "90c853d9-d25f-40ac-940f-76e07c756734"}','[0.044207063,0.03206695,0.023004524,-0.02918012,0.00079592,-0.033954542,-0.0017147878,-0.054694477,0.007314466,0.030115131,-0.03796799,-0.0944499,0.019563211,-0.014033202,-0.052564293,-0.00071875605,0.021227682,0.051633507,-0.006824506,0.05773492,0.00023279765,0.06365742,-0.002652502,-0.06797384,0.014640665,0.016474377,0.05039006,0.015831612,-0.09796594,0.0069624777,0.031603683,0.03484166,-0.005243573,0.027843498,-0.00046521932,0.065225065,0.030452855,0.0017659734,0.019642835,-0.0048498116,0.002125384,-0.01135348,-0.023139946,0.03163944,0.007187118,-0.012376359,0.024723198,-0.019586956,-0.02720629,-0.03249527,0.05393541,-0.0468082,0.019346902,0.02175928,0.011684402,0.00751811,-0.024007013,0.024261933,-0.012716143,0.04260401,-0