	 ('5b48dd2d-22d0-45d5-bd74-683c09bd5460'::uuid,'The Mayor''s daughter was very jealous and purposely had her dad reap Lucy Gray.

The day of the 10th Hunger Games, Coriolanus walks into the Control room with Communicuffs for sending sponsors, and the Dean warns him to find the other mentor a seat near the door. The host introduces himself and shows that he has an envelope with his predicted winner, which he''ll open once the Games end. The tributes enter the arena to see a beaten up tribute hung on a beam in the middle of the arena. Seeing this, the other mentor smashes a chair into the image and runs out of the room, shouting that everyone there is a monster.

The host starts the countdown and the Games begin. Most tributes runs to the Cornucopia as Lucy Gray desperately calls for Jessup. She gets attacked several times by other tributes but successfully takes him to the tunnels, against Coriolanus''s wishes. Following them are two tributes, who are then chased by an alliance. Lucy Gray gets through a slot in the wall which leads her to another room, while Jessup follows her. One tribute also goes under the slot, hanging onto Jessup’s leg. The alliance reaches the other two tributes, with one being caught in a net and killed. The other tribute, whose body is halfway through the slot, is stabbed.

The bloodbath has ended with several tributes dead. The host starts his weather forecast when a tribute emerges and mercy kills the hung tribute with an ax. Her mentor sends her the first sponsor gift in the history of the Hunger Games. A drone arrives with her gift but crashes into a pole.

The Games have continued for longer than expected, mainly due to the tunnels revealed during the bombing. The host cancels his hotel reservation as two tributes drag another tribute''s corpse from underneath the rubble. The Dean confronts Coriolanus about what he''s going to do after the Games and threatens to still not give him the Victory Prize even if Lucy Gray wins. In the tunnels, Jessup is acting strangely and gets scared of the water Lucy Gray is giving her, a sign of rabies. At night, when Coriolanus is napping in the Academy viewing room, the Head Gamemaker suddenly wakes him up, informing him that the other mentor has snuck into the arena to perform a district tradition of throwing bread crumbs on a fallen comrade. She tells Coriolanus to get the other mentor out of the arena and she might convince his father to give him the Victory Prize.

Coriolanus finds the other mentor after entering the arena, attempting to convince him to leave. The other mentor refuses, saying he wants to be in front of the cameras, but Coriolanus tells him the feed has already been cut. While trying to convince the other mentor to leave, a tribute attacks the pair. Coriolanus tells the tribute he doesn''t want to hurt him, but proceeds to beat him to death when the tribute continues to fight. The two escape while other tributes chase them, nearly making it through the gate with them, and they state Lucy Gray is their next target now.

Coriolanus returns home and tells his cousin about what happened. He tells her that he felt awful during the murder, but then felt powerful. His cousin reminds him that his father only had hate in his eyes, and that Coriolanus doesn''t have to follow in his footsteps to be in charge.

The next day, as the mentors watch the Games, Jessup turns on Lucy Gray as his rabies progresses. Coriolanus gets his mentor to send water to scare him away from Lucy Gray. He falls, landing on rocks and mortally wounding him. Lucy Gray stays with him until he passes. Suddenly, the alliance begins to close in on Lucy Gray, who is now alone.','{"source": "The Hunger Games_ The Ballad of Songbirds & Snakes.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 2, "position": 2, "chunk_index": 2, "total_chunks": 4, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/The Hunger Games_ The Ballad of Songbirds & Snakes.txt", "parent_document_id": "90c853d9-d25f-40ac-940f-76e07c756734"}','[0.038242143,0.04170342,0.010730994,-0.029713618,-0.0030947183,0.0016141454,0.007293231,-0.04911927,-0.007252084,0.022261666,-0.03635061,-0.104511976,0.023873383,-0.034472834,-0.069087826,-0.0032209482,0.0462801,0.055527896,-0.019584078,0.057449467,-0.0051305406,0.026801547,-0.018047953,-0.06681732,0.040675156,0.04063822,0.045732923,-0.013703527,-0.11514532,0.03315382,0.016775066,0.013963103,-0.014980815,0.025079535,-0.021610936,0.033220768,0.015463184,-0.004053233,0.017804667,0.0023338962,0.010868791,-0.0337452,-0.0031207146,0.030678857,0.006690648,0.006142057,0.04516276,-0.0073621892,-0.017011277,-0.041675705,0.040767398,-0.042837117,-0.0070144897,0.0140329935,0.028044082,0.0030593579,-0.013274825,0.03139576,-0.02232028,0.008185361,-0.02497887,0.021791833,-0.033286918,0.021325245,-0.01451283,-0.024284616,0.043402083,-0.015085548,0.005785946,-0.012752293,0.03747011,-0.0031377105,-0.009724597,0.019489955,0.01532883,-0.005436975,-0.06274325,-0.033879038,-0.01957344,4.1863244e-05,0.022526003,-0.05692767,-0.03689466,-0.036332898,0.009435635,-0.020183852,0.009867404,0.0030607102,0.040488455,-0.0021850509,-0.03874072,0.02210938,-0.0036438508,0.041028462,0.005920897,-0.04606795,0.0038857048,0.022803148,-0.026612649,0.017729098,0.0035628125,0.032389257,-0.044518452,-0.00623005