	 ('a695b5b2-68f9-4ec1-b5c7-afe204ed1257'::uuid,'Panem is a sovereign post-nuclear state and current democratic constitutional republic established sometime after a series of ecological disasters and a global conflict brought about the collapse of modern civilization. It is situated in North America, consisting of a federal district, the Capitol, and thirteen outlying districts.

For years, Panem''s central government operated as a totalitarian dictatorship and police state with society, particularly in the Capitol, modeled on ancient Rome. The outlying districts were subservient to the Capitol, expected to provide services in exchange for protection given by the Capitol''s armies of Peacekeepers, largely to the detriment of the districts'' populace. This unequal relationship was brutally enforced for several years, culminating in a civil war known as the Dark Days.

After three years of conflict, the rebellion collapsed with the apparent destruction of Sector 13, bringing an end to the war. However, unbeknownst to the wider populace of Panem, Sector 13 had survived, having organized a separate peace with the Capitol after securing a significant portion of the Capitol''s stockpile of nuclear weaponry. In accordance with the ceasefire, Sector 13 disengaged from the insurrection and appeared destroyed in exchange for its independence and a non-aggression pact. The remaining districts were quickly subdued with the resulting Treaty of Treason enforcing a harsh peace on them, as well as instituting the Hunger Games, an annual event established as a continual reminder of the failed rebellion. Public executions and whippings, restrictions on civil rights, and mass surveillance became widespread throughout Panem in the following years. Travel and communication between districts were banned.

For the next seventy-four years, the districts endured oppression at the hands of the Capitol through the Hunger Games. Despite the Games'' intended goal of snuffing out future insurrections, they further incited rebellious activity that gradually built up over the decades. By the time of a certain President''s rule, civil unrest was mounting in a number of districts which, following a specific Hunger Games, further escalated despite several brutal crackdowns. This culminated in the Second Rebellion following another Hunger Games, with the districts once again being led by Sector 13 in a revolution to overthrow Panem''s totalitarian government. Within a year, the regime was deposed and Panem was transformed into a democratic constitutional republic.

The name "Panem" derives from the Latin phrase Panem et circenses, which literally translates into "bread and circuses". The phrase itself is used to describe entertainment used to distract public attention from more important matters. Furthermore, by the government providing ample food, entertainment and protection, the citizens would give up their political rights.

According to the Capitol, Panem has a population of 4,556,778 people.

Panem is located on the continent of North America. The administrative center of the country, the Capitol, is located in the Rocky Mountains. Each one of its thirteen outlying districts are situated across the continent and given their large size, cover significant portions of land.

The size of the country is known not to be as large as North America today, given that large areas of land across the world were flooded by rising sea level. Nevertheless, maps of Panem indicate it is about as large as a former contiguous nation, spanning from the east coast to the west coast of North America. Given the territory it covers, Panem''s geography largely resembles that of a former large nation.

For presumably the majority of its history since its founding, Panem was run as a totalitarian dictatorship led by a president who served for life and wielded absolute power over the government and military. The exact details of the national government are unknown, but it is at least known the President possesses a cabinet, with ministers that presumably oversee different areas of the government.

The government overall is modeled after that of ancient Rome, reflected in Capitol society by the citizenry taking names of Greco-Roman origin and the architecture of the city.','{"source": "Panem.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 0, "position": 0, "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 6, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Panem.txt", "parent_document_id": "359f8d3e-bc90-4d4a-b093-54d368813ce8"}','[-0.03523436,0.118284725,-0.055062678,0.036007013,0.027366146,-0.03729028,-0.0702049,0.04105896,-0.021156073,-0.024751995,-0.04346902,-0.07856265,0.060768068,-0.028933527,0.028973933,-0.017798182,0.026786037,0.026071439,-0.024517132,0.038530502,0.011902389,0.02392396,0.0096047,-0.029241443,-0.008282255,0.0024692125,-0.008969071,0.003268768,-0.048075892,-0.017746804,0.044919807,-0.054455288,0.0124448305,0.05854843,-0.0006021756,0.028719492,-0.0015872736,0.01872001,-0.031500734,0.017285947,0.017021114,-0.012173123,-0.0026782814,0.04831867,-0.012495558,0.0014712451,0.015276764,0.0015913628,-0.009079994,-0.018340271,0.015886828,-0.045372076,0.029388312,0.026622197,0.06713743,-0.035828736,-0.009865963,0.048246235,0.009601934,0.031805515,-0.018248914,0.015266058,-0.0152850645,-0.015188202,-0.006043745,-0.014906746,-0.021189028,-0.0148858605,-0.03905942,0.0019570072,0.037145395,-0.029067434,0.0061758407,-0.010568679,-0.016594872,-0.038286787,-0.033953194,-0.046473764,0.013797704,-0.004502006,0.014473571,0.0074079097,-0.024101347,-0.006970718,0.042899374,-0.04741286,0.0005972351,-0.023291137,-0.0016727317,-0.022532154,-0.014370651,0.010334085,0.0052672434,0.02542484,0.035767816,-0.028913984,0.019477647,-0.03161714,-0.0037115887,0.008925005,-0.015020656,0.0037774318,-0.031073727,-0.0012397111,-0.015135471,0.013039258,-0.043110363,-0.0047723004,-0.004615159,-0.026715877,0.0013871656,0.012610585,0.018743295,-0.002163576,-0.0041591595,-0.045338325,7.97739e-05,0.013916,0.03558909,0.050126523,-0.0034297656,0.015041363,-0.01710167,0.04