	 ('51036161-457c-4fa4-983f-22cc4f40e7ec'::uuid,'Mara Lila Brant was a Minstrels girl from District 7.

She was sixteen years old and her occupation was rebel. Her home was The Gutter in District 7. Her gender was female. Her eye color was dappled green in the book and dark brown in the film. Her hair was auburn in the film.

She was a Minstrels girl. Her mother died in childbirth, so she was raised by her adoptive uncles. She did not know who her father was. She met another character when they were ten years old. At age twelve, she was arrested twice for rebellious acts. Since she was a Baird, she likely had knowledge of a previous victor but did not want to discuss it. She would add scraps of that victor''s dress to her wardrobe as a way to honor her memory.

She was dating another character by the time of the 50th Hunger Games. She taught his younger brother about the stars. She gifted him a striker that she had designed. During the reaping, she and the other character were presumed safe after the four tributes were picked. However, when the last tribute ran away and was killed, a riot broke out. She tried to help his mother prevent Sentinel Corps from taking his body away. The other character tried to protect her and was thus reaped to take the runaway''s place in the Hunger Games. An official demanded that the area was cleaned up and ordered a Peacekeeper to kill her for her resistance. Another official intervened as he wanted to record her tears for the audience. However when they reenacted the reaping, she refused to cry for entertainment. At the conclusion of the reaping, a Peacekeeper was about to put her in handcuffs when her uncles bribed him to let her go. Although she wanted to go over to the other character, they led her away.

Shortly before the train left District 7 for The Central City with the other character, she went to the hill nearby holding gumdrops that he had sent his brother to give her. She wailed at the wind and let out her pain as the train left. The other character watched out the window.

When training scores were released and the other character only received a low score, she performed forbidden songs on the reaping stage. Her performance drew a crowd of other discontented kids, so she was arrested and held on the Sentinel Corps'' base. After the tributes'' interviews, an official arranged a phone call between her and the other character. She told him about her arrest and claimed she would be released; however, she was still incarcerated when he returned home two weeks later. Her uncles arranged for her to be released on house arrest, and she went to graze her geese in the Glade, where she reunited with him.

Upon reuniting with him after his victory, his mother, younger brother, and she were killed as punishment for his rebellious actions during the Games. In her case, she was given a bag of red gumdrops, shortly after her release, believing it to be a bag he had left for her earlier. However, he realized too late that the new bag had been planted there, filled with poison. Despite their best efforts to stop it and call for help, the poison killed her. With her last words, she urged him not to let the sun rise on the reaping. She was buried in the Minstrels''s secret graveyard beside two other Bairds.

As a result of her death, the other character drove away anyone who could''ve been considered close to him so that they wouldn''t suffer the same horrible fate and became an alcoholic. He would''ve welcomed his death if it wasn''t for his promise to her that he would somehow keep the sun from rising on the reaping. He spent weeks looking for her grave, eventually finding it with help and spent two days at her graveside.','{"source": "Lenore Dove Baird.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 0, "position": 0, "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 2, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Lenore Dove Baird.txt", "parent_document_id": "76267fd4-af4c-4fa6-a796-687d7ada1bba"}','[0.019043973,0.050326865,0.028918557,-0.026206236,0.011817859,-0.022143085,0.022449322,-0.026065012,-0.054128617,0.011505481,-0.02097065,-0.05861129,0.01269379,-0.04584229,-0.06549977,-0.00045037788,0.0585353,0.027452132,0.015852902,0.08469706,0.0027154197,0.027412921,0.025757674,-0.06486756,0.050195105,-0.0055343327,0.0014625594,0.038509946,-0.11351512,0.011606123,0.034412,0.0075809075,0.012446231,0.01574175,0.024819143,0.014691389,0.004588442,0.020179806,0.018021049,-0.03425656,0.021598833,0.04513183,-0.028882226,0.015403352,-0.028980251,-0.022326788,0.027165134,-0.028007507,0.005528136,-0.04626576,-0.006393409,-0.036081355,-0.015503012,0.0067403587,0.05145277,0.015474026,-0.00031274345,0.03254095,-0.01587566,-0.010539842,-0.014833303,-0.0006734069,-0.023691753,-0.005809258,-0.00835767,-0.03237851,-0.019486807,-0.032335963,-0.017824404,0.028191168,0.017960928,-0.0035442114,0.022984883,-0.0072380607,0.03631779,-0.036524467,-0.07750083,-0.04519595,-0.01253193,0.01134602,0.0042643026,-0.0013024373,-0.017308323,-0.029642599,-0.0065004,-0.03604493,-0.034275275,0.0032857733,-0.04378496,-0.02922062,-0.013614269,0.018596593,-0.024228737,0.030900752,0.025048047,-0.069510974,-0.017718045,-0.0114253415,-0.035038114,0.009963507,0.003226743,0.050703537,0.0044840327,