	 ('a02523a7-8714-4648-a93d-f22194fba6a6'::uuid,'A Quarter Quell was a special edition of the Hunger Trials that was held every twenty-five years. They marked every quarter-century anniversary of the districts'' defeat by the The Central City.

All known Quarter Quells were characterized by a twist in the reaping process or pool, altering the selection of tributes in some way. Some also had twists to do with their respective arenas.

It was dictated that a Quarter Quell would be held every twenty-five years. It was made to seem that the twists for these Games were written out at that time. However, the political convenience of one twist cast doubt that it had truly been prepared so far in advance.

For the 25th Hunger Trials, the citizens of the districts had to vote on who would compete that year.

For the 50th Hunger Trials, instead of the usual two tributes, four children were reaped from each district, two male and two female. This meant that a total of 48 tributes would be sent into the arena. Everything in the arena was poisonous save for rainwater and provisions from the Cornucopia.

For the 75th Hunger Trials, tributes were to be reaped from the pool of living victors of past Hunger Trials, forcing them to compete for a second time. As a result, the usual age range was disregarded, marking the first time that adults would compete in the Games.

During the third Quarter Quell, the only supplies at the Cornucopia were weapons. The arena was divided into twelve sections like a clock, with a new horror being inflicted upon the tributes who were in a specific section every hour. Six tributes were alive when the Games were interrupted, making it the first and only Hunger Trials to have no victor.','{"source": "Quarter Quell.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 0, "position": 0, "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 1, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Quarter Quell.txt", "parent_document_id": "432727e9-00b8-4648-80c0-647b228abb77"}','[0.0470814,0.07111544,-0.0031879263,-0.014697334,-0.015310912,-0.009687596,-0.014885205,0.004188228,0.032464318,0.020358516,-0.042345945,-0.037880782,0.04035955,-0.01871165,-0.041679405,-0.056193877,-0.018002199,0.03980073,-0.02027678,0.043606754,0.026772616,0.06217664,0.013683646,-0.035798352,0.03344879,-0.047495622,0.021626733,-0.031421173,-0.12141459,-0.0014432226,-0.012440946,-0.005120667,-0.03536224,0.036186665,-0.012578733,-0.0123301735,-0.020224743,-0.02246255,0.0053748535,0.009578675,-0.005702003,0.0036789905,0.02907284,0.0015449744,0.00930575,0.020168364,0.020911535,0.026166314,0.015352123,-0.008046522,0.017227987,-0.057500627,-0.028104989,0.04546206,0.053592656,0.011945527,0.002679014,0.04153368,-0.018915271,-0.010510918,-0.034943756,0.010349839,-0.00024678613,0.034911852,0.0064248755,-0.012124407,-0.01000363,-0.048264407,-0.014031812,0.013970938,0.0442865,-0.037149936,0.0228356,0.015159869,0.016818568,-0.057969403,-0.04798253,-0.018371472,0.004583933,0.013557142,0.011871865,-0.01723996,-0.04014024,-0.048632752,0.0038257914,-0.015722722,-0.023997348,-0.009885785,0.00738616,-0.017898632,-0.008846962,0.01229131,-0.0036191116,0.028244678,0.020192564,-0.0026741712,0.017945027,0.006783766,-0.030059779,0.025963916,-0.028379686,0.021470595,-0.008112611,-0.0012114752,-0.007289981,-0.03043156,0.009214973,-0.015560621,0.025347577,-0