	 ('c683de26-5fb9-4178-8b0b-ca4b5e9c5c38'::uuid,'He poisons the Academy dean, the first victim of his signature method of dispatching his enemies.

The main character is one of the 24 mentors assigned for the 10th Hunger Trials. His family was once powerful but has since fallen on hard times. He is assigned to mentor the female tribute from the lowest district. He becomes embroiled in the ongoing conflict and must face matters of love, chaos, and control. His tribute is a talented singer and part of a performance group. She makes a dramatic entrance into the Hunger Trials and later becomes her district''s first victor. She and the mentor fall in love, but upon finding out who he really is, she attempts to run away, setting a trap for him. The dean of the Academy is credited for creating the Games. He has a dark secret in his past and seems to bear a grudge against the main character. Another mentor is from a district himself and still sympathizes with those in the districts. His father is a powerful war profiteer who bought his family a new life in the Capitol but struggles against his son''s rebellious ways. The main character''s cousin has lived with his family from a very young age. They are like close siblings, and she worries over him as the family''s financial situation worsens. The grandmother of the main character is a regal woman who sings the Capitol anthem and grows roses. She dotes on him and often speaks of the family grandeur. However, as the family struggles to mask their poor financial situation, she begins to descend into denial. The Head Game Master of the 10th Hunger Trials works in the experimental weapons division and is also a top professor at the University. She believes that people are inherently violent and is convinced that war is eternal and must be managed. The tribute''s old boyfriend ditches her for a much richer partner, and upon learning he was dating them both, the partner ordered her father to call out the tribute''s name in the reaping.','{"source": "The Ballad of Songbirds and Snakes.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 2, 