	 ('127eb9b1-54e3-438d-93f9-b442a338c62e'::uuid,'He believes he is dying in the blast.

He wakes up confused to find himself alive, kept in solitary confinement. He is eventually taken for a victor''s ceremony, where a highly edited version of events is presented, erasing all his attempts at sabotage. The nation''s leader crowns him. He is sent back to his district with the bodies of his fallen allies. Upon arriving home, he finds his family home on fire with his mother and brother inside; he is restrained from entering. He attends their funeral and is directed to a special village for winners.

He goes to find his girlfriend, who had been under house arrest. They have a happy reunion, but she eats poisoned candy given to her as punishment and dies in his arms. Haunted, he isolates himself, drinks heavily, and withdraws from the world. He is later taken on a mandatory victory tour, where the cameraman again pitches the idea of rebellion, but the boy rejects him. He returns to his home, knowing his future will to mentor new tributes sent to their deaths each year.

An epilogue reflects on the boy seeing a young girl grow up in his district. He is initially reluctant but finally tells his story to her and another boy ..','{"source": "Sunrise on the Reaping.txt", "charset": "UTF-8", "chunk_id": 1, "position": 1, "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 2, "source_document": "/Users/artem/IdeaProjects/practicum/sprint07/ragbot/./data/replaced/Sunrise on the Reaping.txt", "parent_document_id": "a486ced4-2bf1-4430-87a6-e8815cfdca77"}','[0.03494227,0.081325114,0.031964745,-0.011765775,-0.019279787,-0.031660132,0.020840444,0.032484885,-0.005551377,0.004347498,-0.056073938,-0.042634226,0.020191515,-0.04631006,-0.05508554,-0.0071825264,0.05495357,0.025886461,0.006426521,0.05710839,-0.021082185,0.026799139,-0.031203536,-0.09389383,0.034965746,0.0012820638,0.027376026,-0.019659176,-0.10681506,0.0010959707,0.021841863,0.025530504,-0.009367905,0.03702059,0.022110868,0.01677794,0.00083097554,0.028847793,0.002062256,-0.019625178,0.0029099227,0.008648477,0.020165516,-0.00088490214,-0.007847626,0.00248438,0.00622238,-0.019534033,-0.013078421,-0.025083417,-0.013756443,-0.025973868,-0.008380214,0.025530053,0.04223676,0.004033015,0.015802117,0.028245002,-0.029673934,0.027225638,-0.01713354,0.00042178773,-0.017706098,0.029915303,-0.00094885426,-0.0128673855,0.008741432,-0.006806082,-0.028089536,0.020152934,0.004127345,-0.015086837,0.029372083,0.012261492,0.017045494,-0.036199156,-0.05679416,-0.04322714,-0.021993676,0.016237712,0.0045236805,-0.013304879,-0.0530808,-0.040767156,-0.0057244874,-0.031939168,-0.013880484,0.001609613,0.009214031,-0.008535748,-0.024269683,-0.006171667,-0.0028847593,0.035605606,0.00091316784,0.007533085,-0.012188524,0.019998968,-0.024782246,-0.0043119374,0.012472054,0.03256002,0.0057317223,0.01789233,-0.0068597663,-0.0042200363,-0.004360426,-0.03847533,0.004591466,-0.033385046,-0.008747914,-0.025979588,-0.0019021851,0.025905801,-0.022265913,0.0016431183,-0.0010369008,0.025645982,0.020262627,0.059089262,0.02505814,0.0022795699,-0.